hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Maiz back four times."
"1802","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed preemption so long as it is undivided, with its boundaries marked."
"1803","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zama narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet but that he pastured."
"1804","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salama informed me that he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then revelation paused from me for a while, and while I was walking, there was the angel who had come to me in the cave of Hira, upon a seat between heaven and earth, so I was terrified of him, and I came to Khadija and said: Wrap me, wrap me. So I was wrapped, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came and struck with his foot: {O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify, and defilement shun}. Abu Salama said: And al-rujz is the idols they worshipped besides Allah."
"1805","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: Muadh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and pray with his people."
"1806","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said while preaching: When one of you comes on Friday while the imam is preaching, let him pray two rakas."
"1807","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold a mudabbar slave."
"1808","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, who said: We used to practice withdrawal in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Quran descended upon him. So I said: Did you hear it from Jabir? He said: No."
"1809","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr, who heard Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: War is deception."
"1810","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zama narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to magnify Allah when lowering and when rising."
"1811","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the meat of donkeys and fed us horse meat."
"1812","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy him from me? So Nuaym bought him for eight hundred. Jabir said: A Coptic boy who died the previous year."
"1813","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Maymun al-Makki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five uqiyas."
"1814","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: Did you hear Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will exit the Fire through intercession? Amr said: Yes."
"1815","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will exit the Fire through intercession, then enter Paradise."
"1816","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Bakkar al-Laythi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with dates, for nabidh."
"1817","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I married a woman in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), previously married, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why not a virgin whom you sport with and who sports with you, whom you laugh with and who laughs with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed and left sisters dependent upon me, so I disliked marrying a young girl, but married a woman to look after them. He said: May Allah bless you."
"1818","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I disliked marrying an inexperienced young girl like them, but a woman to comb them and look after them. He said: You did right."
"1819","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: A man of the Emigrants shoved a man of the Ansar with his backside, so the Ansari said: O Ansar. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with the call of ignorance? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he shoved him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, for it is foul."
"1820","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, saying: I heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was ill, breathed upon my face, and I recovered, and the verse of obligation was revealed: {They seek your ruling; say, Allah rules for you concerning kalala}."
"1821","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir say: I sought entry upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Who is it? So I said: I. So he said: I, I, disliking that."
"1822","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir say: When my father was brought on the day of Uhud, and my aunt came weeping over him, I began to weep, and the people began to forbid me while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Weep over him or do not weep over him; by Allah, the angels did not cease shading him with their wings until you buried him."
"1823","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dead, and kissed his forehead."
"1824","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever the believer shields his honor with is charity for him."
"1825","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, that a Bedouin man arrived in Madina and pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then fell ill, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Release me, release me, twice or thrice. He said: Then he left, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed he had left, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madina expels its filth, and its goodness shines forth."
"1826","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace that pleased me, so I said: Whose is this? It was said: Umar ibn al-Khattab's. So I wished to enter it, but I remembered your jealousy. So Umar wept, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Upon you would I be jealous, O Messenger of Allah?"
"1827","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Warqa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, or Salim Abu al-Nadr, or both, Warqa doubted, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, so I stood at his left, and he placed me at his right, and I saw him pray in a single garment, having crossed its ends."
"1828","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, saying: Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended to command a caller to call for prayer, then remain behind against men who stay behind from prayer, and burn their houses over them."
"1829","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best deeds are faith in Allah and striving in the path of Allah. He said: We said: What is the righteousness of Hajj? He said: Feeding food and good speech."
"1830","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw the wife of Abu Talha, and heard a footfall before me, so I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: Bilal."
"1831","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked anything at all and said no."
"1832","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and saw a man shaded over, so he asked, and they said: Fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not of righteousness."
"1833","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hasan say: When al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf arrived he used to delay prayer, so we asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about prayer times, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday, or when the sun declines, pray Asr while the sun is high, pray Maghrib when the sun sets, and pray Isha, sometimes delaying and sometimes hastening: when people gathered he hastened, and when they were late he delayed; and he used to pray Fajr in darkness. Abu Dawud said: Thus Shuba said."
"1834","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abu Tayba and he cupped him, and said: How much is your tax? He said: Three sas. So he reduced a sa from him."
"1835","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that a man come to his family at night."
"1836","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Jabir say: I sold a camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he weighed and gave extra. Some of those dirhams remained with me until they were lost on the day of al-Harra."
"1837","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muharib, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, while I was upon a camel, and he said to me: O Jabir, have you married? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or previously married? I said: Previously married. He said: What is with you and maidens and their play."
"1838","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Jabir say: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we arrived in Madina he said to me: Come to the mosque and pray two rakas in it."
"1839","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muharib, who said: I heard Jabir say: A man of the Ansar with two water-carrying camels reached Muadh while he prayed Maghrib, and Muadh began with Surah al-Baqara or al-Nisa, Shuba said: Muharib doubted. When the man saw that, he prayed, then left. Word reached the man that Muadh says: He is a hypocrite. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah said: O Muadh, are you a trial-maker, are you a trial-maker, are you a trial-maker, or he said: a tempter. Did you not recite: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} or {By the night when it covers} or {By the sun and its brightness}, Shuba said: Muharib doubted. Behind you pray the needy, the young, or he said: the weak. Muharib doubted."
"1840","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad. Shuba said: And Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, saying: I said to Jabir: How many were you on the day of the Tree? He said: We were fifteen hundred, and he mentioned thirst that befell them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought water in a vessel, placed his hand in it, and water began to gush from between his fingers as springs. He said: So we drank, and it sufficed and covered us. He said: I said: How many were you? He said: Had we been a hundred thousand it would have sufficed us; we were fifteen hundred."
"1841","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrate from Jabir, who said: A boy was born to a man of the Ansar, and they wished to name him al-Qasim, but the Ansar refused, so that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The Ansar did well; name yourselves by my name, but do not take my kunya."
"1842","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves by my name, but do not take my kunya."
"1843","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Salim, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa."
"1844","Yunus narrated to us, Yunus narrated: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment."
"1845","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for me on the night of the camel twenty-five times."
"1846","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers, and whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks."
"1847","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey on a rainy day, and he said: Whoever of you wishes, let him pray in his lodging."
"1848","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram for Hajj, and Suraqa ibn Malik said: Inform us about our religion, as if we were created for it now: do we act according to what the pens have written and decrees have passed, or do we begin anew? He said: According to what the pens have written. Zuhayr said: Then Abu al-Zubayr spoke a word I did not understand, so I said to Yasin al-Zayyat: What did he say? He said: Act, for each is eased."
"1849","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with his companions at Nakhl, and the polytheists intended them, then said: Leave them, for they have a prayer after this dearer to them than their children. So Jibril descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. So he prayed Asr with his companions, arranging them in two rows, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before them and the enemy before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They all magnified and all bowed, then those next to him prostrated while the others stood. When they raised their heads, the others prostrated. Then these advanced and these retreated. They all magnified and all bowed, then those next to them prostrated while the others stood. When they raised their heads, the others prostrated."
"1850","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Abi al-Aliya narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba, the muzaffat, the naqir, and the hantam."
"1851","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating sacrificial meat after three days, then addressed us and said: Eat, feed, and store. He said: So we made washiqa from it and carried it to Madina."
"1852","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud: In the name of Allah, and by Allah; greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I testify there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; I ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge with Him from the Fire."
"1853","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was ill, and said to me: O Jabir, I see you dying of this illness of yours, so clarify what is for your sisters. So he bequeathed two thirds for them. He said: Jabir used to say: This verse was revealed concerning me: {If there are two females, for them is two thirds}, the verse."
"1854","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, withhold your wealth for yourselves; do not grant it as life-grants, for whoever is granted something for his lifetime, it belongs to him for his lifetime and after his death."
"1855","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from one who heard Jabir. Abu Dawud said: And Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us with Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, three hundred and some ten of us, and provided us a bag of dates, giving us thereof handful by handful. When we exhausted it he gave us date by date. We used to suck it as a child sucks and drink water over it. When we lost it we felt its loss. We used to beat leaves with our bows, grind them, and drink water over them, until we were called the army of leaves. While we were upon the seashore, there was a beast like a sand dune called al-anbar. Abu Ubayda said: It is carrion, do not eat it. Then he said: The army of the Messenger of Allah in the path of Allah, and we are compelled. He said: So we ate from it twenty nights, or he said: fifteen nights, and made washiqa from it. Twelve men of us sat upon the socket of its eye, and Abu Ubayda took a rib of its ribs, saddled the stoutest camel among the camels of the people with it, and passed under it. He said: When we arrived to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: What detained you? We said: O Messenger of Allah, we followed the caravans of Quraysh, and mentioned to him the affair of the beast, and he said: It is but provision Allah provided you; have you anything of it? So we said: Yes."
"1856","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Sad ibn Muadh for his wound."
"1857","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Sad ibn Muadh for his wound, then stanched it with an arrowhead, so it swelled, then stanched it a second time."
"1858","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for an injury in his hip, or he said: in his back."
"1859","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man freed a slave of his after his death, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Have you anything besides him? He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy him from me? So Nuaym bought him for eight hundred dirhams. He handed him the price and said: Spend upon yourself; if a surplus remains, then upon your kin; if a surplus remains, then here and here and here. And Abu Dawud gestured with his hand before him, to his right, and to his left."
"1860","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban."
"1861","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes my name, let him not take my kunya, and whoever takes my kunya, let him not take my name."
"1862","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the naqir, the muzaffat, and the dubba."
"1863","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have nabidh made for him in a waterskin."
"1864","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A townsman shall not sell for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah providing some of them from others."
"1865","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, who said: I said to him: Did Jabir narrate to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Quhafa: Change it, and avoid black? So he said: No."
"1866","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of severe heat, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, prolonging the standing until they began to fall. He said: Then he bowed and prolonged, then rose and prolonged, then bowed and prolonged, then rose and prolonged, then prostrated twice, then stood and did likewise. So it was four bowings and four prostrations. He kept moving forward and moving backward in his prayer. Then he turned to his companions and said: Paradise and Hell were displayed to me; Paradise drew near to me until had I taken a bunch from it my hand fell short of it, or he said: I attained it, Hisham doubted. And Hell was displayed to me, so I kept retreating fearing it would overwhelm you. And I saw a tall black Himyari woman tormented for a cat of hers: she tied it, neither fed nor watered it, nor let it eat of the vermin of the earth. And I saw therein Abu Thumama Amr ibn Malik dragging his intestines in the Fire. They used to say: The sun and moon eclipse only for the death of a great one; they are two signs among the signs of Allah, mighty and majestic, shown to you. When they eclipse, pray until it clears."
"1867","And Abu Dawud mentioned, from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, live as you will, for you shall die; love whom you love, for you shall part from him; and do as you will, for you shall meet it."
"1868","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people gather then disperse without remembrance of Allah and prayer upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except they rise from the foulest corpse."
"1869","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Bakkar al-Laythi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins with dates for nabidh, and mixing unripe dates with dates."
"1870","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Bakkar narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Zubayr narrate from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar, Bakkar said: and I think he mentioned Uthman, ate meat, then prayed without performing ablution."
"1871","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade handing over a sword unsheathed."
"1872","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talib ibn Habib ibn Amr ibn Sahl, the bedfellow of Hamza, narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari say: Jabir went out on the day of al-Harra and his foot was struck by a stone. He said: Perish whoever frightens the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: And who frightens the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frightens this tribe of the Ansar has frightened what is between these two, meaning his sides."
"1873","Talib said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of those of my Ummah who die, after the decree of Allah, His writ, and His predestination, die by souls, meaning by the evil eye."
"1874","Talib said: And Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: We, Banu Salima, wished to move from our dwellings, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remain firm, for you are its pegs, and there is no servant who steps a step toward prayer but that a reward is written for him thereby."
"1875","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man narrates a narration while turning, it is a trust."
"1876","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from some family of Jabir, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat melon with fresh dates, saying: They are the two most wholesome."
"1877","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from a man, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I grant no protection to one who kills after taking the blood money."
"1878","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kharija ibn Musab narrated to us, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no continual fasting in fasting."
"1879","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Yaman Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, from Abu Abs, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no continual fasting in fasting."
"1880","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan al-Qaysi narrated to us, from a man of Banu Yashkur, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Aslam, may Allah grant it peace."
"1881","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Yaman Abu Hudhayfa and Kharija ibn Musab narrated to us; as for Kharija, he narrated to us from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir, and as for al-Yaman, he narrated to us from Abu Abs, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no suckling after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no freeing except after ownership, no divorce except after marriage, no oath in severing kinship, no Bedouin life after emigration, no emigration after the conquest, no oath for a child against a parent, no oath for a woman against her husband, no oath for a slave against his master, and no vow in disobedience to Allah. Were a Bedouin to perform ten pilgrimages then emigrate, a pilgrimage would be due upon him if he finds a way to it. Were a boy to perform ten pilgrimages then reach puberty, a pilgrimage would be due upon him if he finds a way to it. Were a slave to perform ten pilgrimages then be freed, a pilgrimage would be due upon him if he finds a way to it."
"1882","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man is absent, let him not come to his family at night."
"1883","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from a man of Banu Salima, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when distress befell him on the day of the Confederates, cast off his cloak, stood bared, raised his hands extended, supplicated, and did not pray. He said: Then he came to us, did likewise, and prayed."
"1884","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, saying: Abu Qaza al-Bahili, whose name is Suwayd ibn Hujayr, narrated to me, from Muhajir al-Makki, who said: I said to Jabir: Does a man raise his hands when he looks at the Kaba? He said: I did not think any did this except the Jews. We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); would we do it?"
"1885","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Jabir, who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to Banu Salima; had we shot, we would see the landing places of our arrows."
"1886","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Harmalah, from Abu al-Musabbih al-Himsi, he said: We were marching on a summer expedition while Malik ibn Abdullah al-Khath'ami was in command of the people, and he came upon Jabir as he was walking and leading his mule, and said to him: Will you not ride when Allah has carried you? Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, Allah will forbid him to the Fire. And I am tending my beast and wish to be independent of my people. So the people leapt down from their mounts, and I never saw more dismounted men than on that day."
"1887","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believing man or believing woman, no Muslim man or Muslim woman, who falls ill with an illness, except that Allah the Mighty and Majestic removes his sins on account of it."
"1888","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Vinegar, what an excellent condiment it is."
"1889","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Mubashshir while she was in her palm grove, and said: Who planted this, a disbeliever or a believer? She said: O Messenger of Allah, rather a believer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believer who plants a plant or sows a crop, and a beast or a wild animal or a bird eats from it, except that it is charity for him."
"1890","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise eat and drink therein; they do not spit, blow their noses, urinate, or defecate; the need of one of them is only a belch with a scent like the scent of musk."
"1891","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? He said: That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand. Or he said: He from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then which martyrs are most excellent? He said: That your horse be hamstrung and your blood be shed. He said: Then which prayer is most excellent? He said: Lengthy standing in devotion."
"1892","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the people of Ta'if said: O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land, so what suffices us for the bath of janabah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour water over my head three times."
"1893","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say three days before his death: Let none of you die except while he thinks well of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"1894","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, he said: I heard Nubayh al-Anazi narrating from Jabir, that the slain of Uhud were carried from their resting places when they were killed, and then a caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Return the slain to their resting places. And Abu Dawud once said: To the places where they fell. He said: When I paid the man in full the dates that were owed to him by my father, I came running as if I were a spark."
"1895","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it becomes ripe. It was asked: What is its becoming ripe? He said: That it turns red and yellow."
"1896","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mina al-Makki narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhabarah."
"1897","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbir over the Negus four times."
"1898","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My example and your example is like that of a man who kindled a fire, and grasshoppers and moths came falling into it while he drives them away from it; and I am holding you by your waist-wrappers lest you plunge into the Fire, while you slip away from my hand."
"1899","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My example and the example of the Prophets is like that of a man who built a house, and completed and perfected it, except for the place of one brick; whoever entered it and looked at it would say: How beautiful it is, except for the place of this brick! So I am the place of the brick; the Prophets were sealed with me."
"1900","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar, he heard al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to come to his family by night, until the disheveled woman combs herself and the woman whose husband is absent removes unwanted hair."
"1901","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal informed me, he said: I read to al-Sha'bi a letter from Jabir ibn Abdullah in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. Al-Sha'bi said: I heard this from Jabir."
"1902","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I sold a camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he lent me its back to ride on for my journey to Medina."
"1903","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Suhayb al-Faqir, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abdullah about the two rak'ahs in travel, should I shorten them? Jabir said: The two rak'ahs in travel are not a shortening; shortening is only one rak'ah in battle. He said: Then he began to narrate that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the time of battle when the prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and lined up a group behind him, while another group stood facing the enemy, and he prayed one rak'ah with them and performed two prostrations with them; then those who had prayed behind him went and took the place of the others, and the others came and lined up behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed one rak'ah with them and performed two prostrations with them; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and gave the salam, and those behind him gave the salam, and the others gave the salam; so it was two rak'ahs for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one rak'ah each for the people. Then Yazid recited: And when you are among them and lead them in prayer."
"1904","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is ablution, and the key to Paradise is prayer."
"1905","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamzah ibn Suhayb, he said: I saw Wahb ibn Kaysan prostrating upon the forelock of hair, so I asked him about that and he said: Jabir narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so."
"1906","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah say: I said to Jabir ibn Abdullah: Ibn al-Zubayr forbids mut'ah while Ibn Abbas enjoins it. Jabir said: The hadith circulated at my hands; we performed tamattu' in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then when Umar came he addressed us and said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic used to permit His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whatever He willed, and the Qur'an has been revealed in its various circumstances, so separate your Hajj from your Umrah, and definitively sever marriage with these women; no man who marries a woman for a fixed term shall be brought to me except that I will stone him."
"1907","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: Talhah passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: A martyr walking upon the face of the earth."
"1908","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your deeds are presented to your clansmen and relatives in their graves; if it is good they rejoice at it, and if it is otherwise they say: O Allah, inspire them to act in obedience to You."
"1909","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman al-Yashkuri, from Jabir, he said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah seventy cows or seventy camels; a cow was on behalf of seven."
"1910","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Rashid, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plastering a grave or building over it."
"1911","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"1912","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: Jabir narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon his mount toward the east voluntarily, and when he intended the obligatory prayer he descended and faced the qiblah."
"1913","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate fresh dates with them and drank water, and said: This is among the bliss about which you will be asked."
"1914","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray during a battle toward the east upon his mount."
"1915","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with a sa'. Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said to him: My hair is abundant. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more abundant hair than you, and better."
"1916","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: While Ubayd ibn Umayr was narrating and Ibn Umar was with him, Ibn Umayr said in his narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two enclosures; when it comes to these they butt it, and when it comes to those they butt it. Ibn Umar said: That is not so; he only said: Between two flocks. They differed over two flocks and two enclosures, and Ibn Umar became agitated and said: Had I not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would not have spoken."
"1917","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us: He said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Nawfal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever abandons prayer, it is as if he has been bereaved of his family and wealth. Al-Zuhri said: I mentioned that to Salim, and he said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons the Asr prayer..."
"1918","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a funeral passes by one of you, let him stand until it leaves him behind."
"1919","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells date-palms that have been pollinated, and the buyer does not stipulate the fruit, then he has nothing of it; and whoever sells a slave who has wealth, and does not stipulate his wealth, then he has nothing of it."
"1920","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what should one in ihram wear? He said: He should not wear a shirt, nor a turban, nor trousers, nor any garment touched by wars or saffron, and he should not wear leather socks unless he cannot find sandals, in which case he should cut them below the ankles."
"1921","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not buy fruits until their soundness becomes evident."
"1922","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereaved of his family and wealth."
"1923","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the keys of the unseen except for five; then he recited this verse: Indeed, with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, to its end."
"1924","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured from you, then estimate for it."
"1925","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim, Musa, and Isa, may Allah's blessings be upon them, at Bayt al-Maqdis, meaning where he was taken on the Night Journey; I saw Musa as a spare-built dark man of medium height, as if from the men of Shanu'ah, and I saw Isa as a reddish man as if just brought out of a bathhouse, and I resemble the sons of Ibrahim most among them; and I was brought a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk, and I took the milk, so Jibril, peace be upon him, said: You have been guided to the fitrah; had you taken the wine your community would have gone astray. Al-Zuhri said: Sa'id used to narrate this to us, and Salim had informed us that his father said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say of Isa: Red; rather he said: I saw myself in a dream as if I were circumambulating the House, and I saw Isa as a man of medium height with water dripping from his head, or water pouring from it, then I turned and there was a reddish man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, his eye like a protruding grape; it was said: This is the Dajjal, the nearest of people in resemblance to Ibn Qatan al-Khuza'i of Banu al-Mustaliq. Al-Zuhri said: And he died in the pre-Islamic period."
"1926","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Usamah is the most beloved of people to me, and he made no exception, neither Fatimah nor anyone else."
"1927","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer is not stung from the same hole twice. Abu Dawud said: He is not punished for his sin in this world and then punished for it in the Hereafter."
"1928","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: I have not sworn by them since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this, neither deliberately nor forgetfully."
"1929","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Mina the travel prayer, two rak'ahs; then Abu Bakr prayed two rak'ahs, then Umar after him prayed two rak'ahs, then Uthman after him prayed two rak'ahs, then Uthman later prayed in full."
"1930","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, or another, from Salim, Abu Dawud doubting, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would indeed command us to lighten the prayer, yet he would lead us in the morning prayer with al-Saffat."
"1931","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the bier."
"1932","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"1933","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. He said: And he was blind, and it would be said to him: Call the adhan, for morning has come."
"1934","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your likeness only. And Ibn Sa'd said: Your remaining among those nations who passed before you is only like the period between the Asr prayer and sunset; the people of the Torah were given the Torah and worked till midday, and were given a qirat each; the Christians were given the Gospel and worked till Asr, and were given a qirat each; and we were given the Qur'an and worked from the Asr prayer till sunset, and were given two qirats each; so the people of the two Books said: Our Lord, You gave us a qirat each though we worked more than they, and You gave them two qirats each? He said: Did I wrong you anything of your wage? They said: No. He said: Then it is My bounty, which I give to whom I will."
"1935","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Budayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in three things: in the house, the woman, and the horse."
"1936","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her, and he said to me: Divorce her, but I refused; so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Divorce her. So I divorced her."
"1937","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar or Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No sooner does Allah the Mighty and Majestic afflict the people of a town or a people with punishment than it encompasses them all; then they will be raised on the Day of Resurrection according to their intentions, or according to their deeds."
"1938","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. And Ibn Umar added: Here I am, here I am; here I am, and at Your service; good is in Your hands; here I am, and longing is to You, and deed."
"1939","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Talhah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined, the woman who tattoos and the woman for whom it is done."
"1940","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray upon his mount while traveling wherever his mount turned, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"1941","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"1942","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"1943","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) built the mosque he made a door for women, and said: No man among the men shall enter through this door. Nafi' said: I never saw Ibn Umar entering through that door nor leaving through it."
"1944","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah ibn Asma' narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there are three people, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."
"1945","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness becomes evident, forbidding both the seller and the buyer from that."
"1946","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dies, his seat in Paradise and his seat in the Fire are shown to him, morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise then of the people of Paradise, and if he is of the people of the Fire then of the people of the Fire."
"1947","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut down the date-palms of Banu al-Nadir and burned, and it is about which Hassan ibn Thabit said: Sarati [text breaks off]."
"1948","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"1949","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for those who shave three times, or twice, and it was said to him: And those who shorten? And he said: And those who shorten."
"1950","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray the two rak'ahs after Friday prayer, nor the two rak'ahs after Maghrib, except with his family."
"1951","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount stood straight with him."
"1952","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You."
"1953","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what should one in ihram wear? He said: He should not wear a shirt, nor a turban, nor trousers, nor leather socks unless he cannot find sandals, in which case let him wear leather socks cut below the ankles, and he should not wear any garment touched by wars or saffron."
"1954","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he used to come to the mosque of Quba riding and walking, and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"1955","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not right for a Muslim man who has wealth concerning which to make a bequest to spend more than two nights, except with his will written with him."
"1956","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"1957","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says to his brother: O disbeliever, then one of them bears it; if the one to whom it was said is a disbeliever then he is a disbeliever, otherwise it returns to the one who said it."
"1958","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sakhr narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque while he was in prayer, and scraped it off while standing; then when he had prayed he expressed anger at the people and said: When one of you is in prayer, Allah the Mighty and Majestic is before his face, so let none of you spit in front of his face during prayer."
"1959","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and it was said to Ibn Awn: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: As for from Ibn Umar, there is no doubt in it. He said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"1960","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he raised it with the like thereof."
"1961","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Talhah narrated to us, from Nafi', he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these eyes of yours? He said: Yes. He said: And did you speak to him with these tongues of yours? He said: Yes. He said: And did you pledge allegiance to him with these right hands of yours? He said: Yes. He said: Glad tidings to you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Shall I not inform you of something I heard from him? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Glad tidings to whoever saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings to whoever did not see me and believed in me, three times."
"1962","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and placed the stone of the ring toward the inside of his palm."
"1963","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas, al-Umari Abdullah ibn Umar, and Abdullah ibn Nafi', all of them, narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off a hand for a shield valued at three dirhams."
"1964","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"1965","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari and Ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah on the day of the conquest of Mecca and closed the door upon himself, and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, Uthman ibn Talhah, Usamah ibn Zayd, and Bilal entered with him; then when they came out I raced the people and outran them, and said to Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars, facing the ..."
"1966","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"1967","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to us, he said: I set out with Ibn Umar to Ibn Abbas concerning a need of Ibn Umar, and he narrated that day, meaning Ibn Umar, that a man greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he did not return it; he went on, and when he was about to disappear he reached for a wall and struck it with his hand, then wiped his face and hands, then did so a second time and wiped to his forearms, then returned the greeting to the man, then said: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was not pure."
"1968","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Which people are best? They said: O Messenger of Allah, a man who gives his wealth and his self. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is a good man, but it is not him; rather the best of people is a man who gives his utmost effort."
"1969","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Let him take her back until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure; for that is the waiting period which Allah the Mighty and Majestic commanded."
"1970","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May Allah forgive Ghifar, and may Allah grant peace to Aslam, and Usayyah who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"1971","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Qur'an, fearing that the enemy might seize it."
"1972","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had committed adultery, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you find in your Book? They said: We do not find stoning. Ibn Salam said: They have lied; stoning is in their Book. He said: So he called for Ibn Suriya, and he began to read until when he reached the place of stoning he placed his hand upon the place of stoning, and Ibn Salam said: Lift your hand. So he lifted it, and there was the verse of stoning. He said: O Muhammad, stoning is in our Book. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had them both stoned at al-Balat. He said: The Jewish man began to shield her with himself."
"1973","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine in this world shall not drink it in the Hereafter, unless he repents."
"1974","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons on Friday, separating between them by sitting."
"1975","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: I was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr but I was not accepted, while I was thirteen years old; I was presented to him on the day of Uhud while I was fourteen and was not accepted; and I was presented to him on the day of the Trench while I was fifteen, and I was accepted."
"1976","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of two sellers, there is no sale between them until they part, unless their sale is a sale with the option."
"1977","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Harb al-Nadbi narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about exchange, a dirham for two dirhams, and he said: It is usury itself, it is usury itself, so do not approach it. Did you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take like for like."
"1978","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, say: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Take her back until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure; if you wish then divorce, and if you wish then keep. Ibn Umar said: So I divorced her, though had I wished I would have kept her."
"1979","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he heard Ibn Umar mention the like thereof."
"1980","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Amr al-Azdi or al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Amr al-Nadbi narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer in travel, and he said: Will you take from me if I narrate to you? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left this city of Medina, he continued to pray two rak'ahs until he returned to it."
"1981","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn al-Arabi narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about crowding at the Stone, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch it and kiss it. So I said: What if I am overpowered or pushed? He said: Put your what-if with that star; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss it and touch it."
"1982","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows and said: It brings no good; by it is only extracted from the miser."
"1983","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman, from Ibn Umar, he said: Ten rak'ahs I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, two rak'ahs after Isha, and two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"1984","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Ka'bah, and there will come one who will forbid you from that, so do not obey him, meaning Ibn Abbas."
"1985","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi', selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars; so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was about to enter the house of Hafsah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I sell camels at al-Baqi', selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in taking them at the rate of the day, so long as you do not part while anything remains between you."
"1986","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, that he witnessed Sa'id ibn Jubayr at Muzdalifah; he called the iqamah and prayed Maghrib three rak'ahs, then gave the salam, then prayed Isha two rak'ahs, then said: Ibn Umar did with us in this place the like of this, and Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did with us in this place the like of this."
"1987","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Sa'id ibn Jubayr at Muzdalifah; he called the iqamah and prayed Maghrib three rak'ahs then gave the salam, and prayed Isha two rak'ahs then gave the salam, and said: Abdullah ibn Umar prayed with us in this place and did the like of this, then narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did the like of this in this place."
"1988","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that upon me, until I divorced her while she was pure."
"1989","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when a bird or a chicken was being shot at, and when they saw Ibn Umar they scattered; so he said: May Allah curse whoever did this; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever did this."
"1990","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while facing toward Khaybar."
"1991","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Mus'ab ibn Sa'd say: They entered upon Abdullah ibn Amir in the illness in which he died, and they began to praise him while Ibn Umar remained silent; so he said: I am not the least sincere of them toward you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah the Mighty and Majestic does not accept charity from misappropriated spoils, nor prayer without purification."
"1992","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Waththab say: I asked Ibn Umar about bathing on Friday, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to do it."
"1993","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Waththab narrating from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whom he deems to be Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer, or the Muslim, who mixes with people and bears their harm patiently is better, or more excellent, than the believer who does not mix with people nor bear their harm patiently."
"1994","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard, and he said: I neither eat it nor forbid it."
"1995","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar, that Umar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about one in janabah sleeping. He said: Wash your private part, perform ablution, then sleep."
"1996","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wars and saffron. I said: For one in ihram? He said: For one in ihram."
"1997","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar say: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, he would dictate to us: As far as you are able."
"1998","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar say: There was a man who was cheated in buying, and he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you buy, say: No deception."
"1999","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of two sellers, there is no sale between them until they part, except a sale with the option."
"2000","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cannot find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers; and whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear leather socks. I said: For one in ihram? He said: For one in ihram."
"2001","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray upon his mount wherever it faced in travel, and he reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so."
"2002","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala' and gifting it. I said: Did you hear it from him yourself? He said: Yes; his son asked him about it."
"2003","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling date-palms until their soundness becomes evident. Ibn Umar said: And its soundness is that it can be eaten from."
"2004","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling food until its owner takes full possession of it."
"2005","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek Laylat al-Qadr; whoever among you seeks it, let him seek it on the night of the twenty-seventh. Or he said: In the last seven."
"2006","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five which one in ihram may kill in the sacred and unsacred territory: the vicious dog, the rat, the crow, the scorpion, and the kite."
"2007","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"2008","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The moon split in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness."
"2009","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit women to pray in the mosque at night."
"2010","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than twenty times reciting in the two rak'ahs after Maghrib and the two rak'ahs before Fajr: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"2011","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women from the mosques at night. His son said: Indeed, by Allah, we shall prevent them; they take it as a covert. So he raised his hand and struck him, and said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say this!"
"2012","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks your protection by Allah, grant him protection; whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever does you a favor, recompense him; and if you find nothing with which to recompense him, praise him until you know that you have recompensed him."
"2013","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, Abu Dawud said: And I remember the narration of al-A'mash better, though the chain is one, they both heard Sa'd ibn Ubaydah narrating from Ibn Umar, that a man asked him about one who swears by the Ka'bah. He said: Do not swear by the Ka'bah, but swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah; for Umar used to swear by his father, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk."
"2014","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Malik say: I witnessed Ibn Umar at Muzdalifah; he prayed Maghrib and Isha, combining them with one iqamah, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in this place."
"2015","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Abi Thabit the blind, from Tamim ibn Iyad, from Ibn Umar, he said: Alqamah ibn Ulathah was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Bilal came to announce the prayer to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Bilal; let Alqamah take sahur. He said: And he was taking sahur with a head."
"2016","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from his father, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I see you crowding to touch these two corners. He said: If I do so, it is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Touching them both removes sins."
"2017","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever circumambulates the House seven times, counting them, a good deed is written for every step, a sin is erased from him, a rank is raised for him, and it equals freeing a slave."
"2018","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns a fourth time, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights, and if he repents Allah will not turn to him, and it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the mud of Khabal. It was asked: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the mud of Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"2019","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Station, performed sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and said: You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"2020","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women from coming to the mosques. His son said: By Allah, we shall surely prevent them. So Ibn Umar said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say this!"
"2021","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Hudayr, from Yazid ibn Utarid, from Ibn Umar, he said: In the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to drink standing and eat while walking briskly."
"2022","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Jabalah ibn Suhaym informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is thus and thus and thus, gesturing with his fingers three times, and withholding the thumb on the third."
"2023","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, he said: Famine struck us, and Ibn al-Zubayr provided us with dates; so Ibn Umar said: Do not eat two dates together, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qiran, unless one of you consults his brother."
"2024","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hantamah. I said to Ibn Umar: What is the hantamah? He said: The jar."
"2025","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from A'idh ibn Nusayb, he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Ka'bah."
"2026","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyib, he said: One who heard Ibn Umar narrated to me, or he said: He asked Ibn Umar, saying: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we are people who hire out our camels, and people say: There is no Hajj for you. So Ibn Umar said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he remained silent until this verse came down: Then when you pour forth from Arafat, remember Allah at al-Mash'ar al-Haram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: You are pilgrims."
"2027","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hayyan al-Bariqi, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar, or a man said to him: I pray behind so-and-so, and he lengthens the prayer? So he said: Two rak'ahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were lighter than one rak'ah of the prayer of so-and-so, or were like the prayer of so-and-so, or like one rak'ah of the prayer of so-and-so."
"2028","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar, the naqir, and the varnished vessel."
"2029","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, he heard Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning Laylat al-Qadr: Seek it in the last ten; if one of you is weak or unable, let him not be overcome regarding the remaining seven."
"2030","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies without an imam dies a death of ignorance, and whoever withdraws his hand from obedience will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for him."
"2031","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The parable of people is like a hundred camels among which a mount suitable for riding can hardly be found."
"2032","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: May Allah forgive Ghifar, and may Allah grant peace to Aslam, and Usayyah are those who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"2033","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"2034","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Umar and Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naqir, muzaffat and dubba vessels."
"2035","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin - and the narration of Hammad ibn Zayd is more complete. Hammad ibn Zayd said: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Tell me about the two rakahs of Fajr, should I prolong the recitation in them? Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, and pray witr with one rakah. I said: That is not what I am asking you about. He said: You are a bulky man; I want to recite the hadith for you fully and you do not let me! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, pray witr with one rakah, and pray the two rakahs as though the call to prayer were between his ears."
"2036","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jasr narrated to us, from Sulayt, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the blast - or from the intense heat - of Hell, so extinguish it from yourselves with cold water."
"2037","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Umar saw a man slaughtering his sacrificial camel, so he said: Slaughter it standing, for it is the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2038","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, Qarn for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen."
"2039","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who vowed to fast on Friday, so he said: We were commanded to fulfill vows, and we were forbidden from fasting this day."
"2040","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar - who is not al-Farra - informed me, from Abu al-Muthanna, from Ibn Umar, he said: The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pronounced twice each phrase, and the iqamah once, except that when the caller said: The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun, he said it twice."
"2041","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution washing each part once, and said: This is the obligatory ablution without which prayer is not valid. Then he performed ablution washing twice each, and said: This is the ablution of one who wishes his reward to be doubled twice. Then he performed ablution washing three times each, and said: This is my ablution and the ablution of the Prophets before me."
"2042","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ulwan Abdullah ibn Ismah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among Thaqif there will be a liar and a destroyer of lives."
"2043","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about witr, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One rakah at the end of the night."
"2044","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Num, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when he was asked about a pilgrim in ihram killing flies, so he said: O people of Iraq, you ask me about a pilgrim in ihram killing flies while you killed the son of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are my two sweet basils in this world."
"2045","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I see you doing things I have not seen anyone else do. He said: Go ahead, for you bring wonders. He said: I saw you dyeing your beard yellow. He said: What else? He said: I saw you touching only the two corners of the House, the Black and the Yemeni, and I saw you not entering ihram until your mount stands upright with you. Ibn Umar said: As for the yellow dye you mentioned, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching his beard with something yellow. As for the two corners, I performed tawaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not see him touching any besides them. And as for entering ihram, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not entering ihram until his mount stood upright with him."
"2046","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Muslim al-Hannat, he said: I heard a man from the people of Iraq asking Ibn Umar, and Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises and the day ascends, and forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets."
"2047","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Muslim al-Hannat, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet the caravans, let no town-dweller sell on behalf of a desert-dweller, and let no man propose over the proposal of his brother until he marries or leaves it."
"2048","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Bariqi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended a journey and mounted his camel, he said Allahu Akbar three times, then said: Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and the two verses. O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine for righteousness and piety, and such deeds as You love and approve. O Allah, shorten for us the distance of the land and make the journey easy for us. O Allah, accompany us in our journey and take care of our families in our absence. And when he returned he said: Returning, repenting, praising our Lord."
"2049","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abdullah narrating from Ibn Umar - Shubah thought it was from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that he said: The prayer of the night and day is two by two."
"2050","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, he said: Muharib ibn Dithar said to me: What did Said ibn Jubayr used to say about al-Kawthar? I said: Said used to narrate from Ibn Abbas that it is abundant good. Muharib said: Where does the opinion of Ibn Abbas fall? Muharib said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: When: Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar, was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: It is a river in Paradise, its banks of gold, flowing over pearls and rubies, its soil more fragrant than musk, its taste sweeter than honey, and its water whiter than snow."
"2051","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muharib ibn Dithar informed me, he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam, muzaffat and jarr vessels."
"2052","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Muharib, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"2053","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Ibrahim Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a man who prays four rakahs before Asr."
"2054","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bakr ibn Abdullah and Bishr ibn Aidh al-Hudhali, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only one who has no share wears silk."
"2055","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, he said: I heard Abu al-Fadl - or Ibn al-Fadl - narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, so accept my repentance, indeed You are the Most Relenting, the Most Forgiving. If a person were to count, he would count a hundred times upon his hand."
"2056","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Zadhadhan saying: I said to Ibn Umar: Tell us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade among vessels; tell us in your language and explain it in ours. He said: He forbade hantam, which is the earthen jar; he forbade muzaffat, which is coated with pitch; he forbade dubba, which is the gourd; he forbade naqir, which is the base of the palm trunk hollowed out and scraped; and he commanded that drinks be prepared in waterskins."
"2057","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard a man from the people of Najran saying: I said to Ibn Umar: I ask you only about two matters, about advance payment for dates on palms and about raisins and dates. He said: As for advance payment for dates on palms, a man once paid in advance for the dates of another man's palms, but they bore nothing that year, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: On what basis does he consume his wealth? And he ordered him to return it to him. Then he forbade advance payment for dates on palms until their soundness appears. As for raisins and dates, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunken man who said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not drink wine, I only drank raisins and dates. So he ordered that the prescribed punishment be applied to him, and he forbade the two being mixed together."
"2058","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Khaliq al-Shaybani, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have drinks prepared for him in a waterskin."
"2059","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah, Hisham and Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so he said: Do you know Ibn Umar, for he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Let him take her back. Hammad added in his narration from Qatadah from Yunus ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Was it counted against you as a divorce? He said: Yes; do you think that if Ibn Umar were helpless and foolish it would not count as divorce?"
"2060","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Kathir ibn Jumhan, he said: I saw Ibn Umar walking in the place of running between al-Safa and al-Marwah, so I asked him about that, and he said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and if I run, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running."
"2061","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I asked al-Shabi about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so he said: She observes waiting by the divorce but not by that menstruation. I say this from the statement of Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2062","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, he said: al-Shabi said to me: What of al-Hasan narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, I sat with Ibn Umar in Madinah for such and such a time and never heard him narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except one hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among some of his Companions when meat was brought, and one of his wives said: Hold back, for it is lizard meat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat it, for it is lawful - or he said: Eat, for there is no harm in it."
"2063","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, he said: I heard Mawriq al-Ijli saying: A man said to Ibn Umar: Tell me about the Duha prayer, do you pray it? He said: No. He said: Did Umar pray it? He said: No. He said: Did Abu Bakr pray it? He said: No. He said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it? He said: I do not think so."
"2064","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Hafs ibn Asim narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer at Mina two rakahs - or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Mina two rakahs, and Abu Bakr two rakahs, and Umar two rakahs, and Uthman two rakahs; then Uthman later prayed the full prayer."
"2065","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Yannaq al-Makki informed me, he said: I witnessed Ibn Umar when he saw a man in Makkah dragging his lower garment, so he said: Who are you? The man traced his lineage, and he turned out to be from Banu Layth, and Ibn Umar recognized him. Ibn Umar said to him: Lift your garment, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine saying: Whoever drags his garment intending nothing thereby but pride, Allah Almighty will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2066","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: Sawwar ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Umar about prayer while traveling, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two rakahs, two rakahs, except Maghrib."
"2067","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Talhah, he said: I heard Abu al-Khasib saying: I was sitting when Ibn Umar came, and a man stood up from his seat for him, but Ibn Umar refused to sit in it. The man kept saying: What harm is there if you sit? What harm is there if you sit? Ibn Umar said: I would not sit in your seat nor in any other's after I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and another stood up from his seat for him and he wanted to sit in it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"2068","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman came to him and said: What is the right of the husband over his wife? He said: She must not withhold herself from him even if she is upon the back of a camel saddle, nor give anything from his house except with his permission; if she does so, he receives the reward and she bears the sin. She must not fast voluntarily except with his permission; if she does, she sins and is not rewarded. And she must not leave his house except with his permission; if she does, the angels curse her - the angels of wrath and the angels of mercy - until she repents or returns. It was said: Even if he is unjust? He said: Even if he is unjust."
"2069","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Sallam narrated that al-Hakam ibn Mina narrated that Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon the wood of his minbar: People shall certainly stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah will surely seal their hearts, then they will surely be recorded among the heedless."
"2070","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said al-Qurashi, a descendant of Said ibn al-As, narrated to us, he said: My father Said informed me, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him, and he said: Who are you? He said: A man from Aslam. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings, O brother of Aslam? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: May Allah forgive Ghifar, and may Allah grant peace to Aslam."
"2071","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn al-Mundhir, he said: We were with a son of Ibn Umar in the garden, and there was a camel skin in the water, and he performed ablution from it. I said: Do you do this? He said: My father narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When water amounts to two qullahs, nothing makes it impure."
"2072","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: We enter upon our rulers and speak something before them, then when we leave we say otherwise. Ibn Umar said: We used to count this as hypocrisy. Al-Umari said: Then my brother narrated to me that Ibn Umar said: We used to count this as hypocrisy in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2073","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Asim, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This authority shall remain among Quraysh so long as even two men remain among people."
"2074","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Tawbah al-Misri, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Three verses were revealed concerning wine. The first to be revealed was: They ask you about wine and gambling, to the end of the verse. It was said: Wine has been forbidden. Then it was said: O Messenger of Allah, let us benefit from it as Allah Almighty said. So he remained silent toward them. Then this verse was revealed: Do not approach prayer while intoxicated. It was said: It has been forbidden. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not drink it near prayer. So he remained silent toward them. Then was revealed: O you who believe, wine and gambling are but, to the end of the verse. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine has been forbidden. He said: A camel-load of wine arrived for a man from Syria - or two camel-loads. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arose, along with Abu Bakr and Umar - and I know Uthman was with them - and they went to the man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it for us to tear open. He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not sell it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed wine, cursed its planter, cursed its drinker, cursed its presser, cursed its shelterer, cursed its server, cursed its pourer, cursed its carrier, cursed the consumer of its price, and cursed its seller."
"2075","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah and Shayban narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Ibn Umar, that he said to a man: As for what you asked me: Did Uthman witness Badr? He was occupied with the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned him his share. As for the Pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the people of Makkah, and had there been anyone more trusted in his view than Uthman he would have sent him; the pledge took place while Uthman was absent, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This hand of mine is for Uthman, and he struck one of his hands upon the other. As for his turning away on the day the two hosts met, I testify that Allah Almighty has pardoned him. Take this with you."
"2076","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Anas narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three qualities, whoever possesses them finds thereby the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than all besides them, that being cast into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, and that a man loves a servant loving him only for the sake of Allah - or he said: in Allah - one of the two; Abu Dawud doubted."
"2077","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2078","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us. Shubah said: Qatadah informed us, and Hisham said: from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no evil omen, and good omens please me. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a good omen? He said: The good word."
"2079","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, so he said: What is this? He said: This is something given in charity to Barirah. He said: It is a gift for us, and charity for her."
"2080","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Prophet but that he warned his people about the one-eyed liar. Verily he is one-eyed, and Allah Blessed and Exalted is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is disbeliever, which every believer reads."
"2081","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant who has good with Allah loves to return to this world, except the martyr, for he wishes he could return and be killed ten times over, because of what he sees of the excellence of martyrdom."
"2082","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh: Know that whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah shall enter Paradise."
"2083","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, while in his heart is goodness weighing a grain of barley; and there shall come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, while in his heart is goodness weighing a grain of wheat; and there shall come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, while in his heart is goodness weighing - Hisham said: an atom - and Shubah said: a millet seed."
"2084","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: If My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and if he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom."
"2085","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned white-speckled rams, pronouncing the name of Allah and magnifying Him; I saw him placing his cheeks upon their sides."
"2086","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a man of the Ansar said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, you appointed so-and-so but did not appoint me. He said: After me you shall see favoritism, so be patient until you meet me at the Basin."
"2087","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals, and Abu Bakr flogged forty. When Umar came and people drew near from the countryside and villages, he said: What do you think about the penalty for wine? Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I think you should make it like the lightest of the prescribed penalties. So Umar flogged eighty."
"2088","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Companions of the Prophet said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book greet us, so how should we return their greeting? He said: Say: And upon you."
"2089","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Permission was granted to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr to wear a shirt of silk."
"2090","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman and al-Zubayr complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, so he permitted them to wear a shirt of silk. Anas said: I saw both of them wearing a shirt of silk."
"2091","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let him not spit before him nor to his right, but to his left and beneath his foot."
"2092","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Anas, he said: I said to him: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes; we asked him about that. He said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), behind Abu Bakr, behind Umar, and behind Uthman, and they used to begin with: All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"2093","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved pumpkin, so when I saw that I began placing it before him."
"2094","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."
"2095","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold, and he approved that."
"2096","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas narrated to us, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse of Abu Talhah called Mandub, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no cause for alarm, and indeed we found him swift as the sea."
"2097","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Abu al-Tayyah, they both heard Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two. And Qatadah added: So neither has precedence over the other."
"2098","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel, so he said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you - or: Fie upon you - ride it."
"2099","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer."
"2100","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second to it, and if he had a second he would seek a third to it, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns to Him. Anas said: I do not know whether it was revealed to him or he used to say it."
"2101","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which none who heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shall narrate to you after me: I heard him saying: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge is lifted, ignorance appears, wine is drunk, adultery appears, men decrease and women increase, until there is one caretaker for fifty women."
"2102","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman were upon Hira, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, for upon you are only a Prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr."
"2103","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a woman seized a slave girl who had jewelry with her, crushed her head between two stones, and took the jewelry. That was referred to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he crushed her head between two stones."
"2104","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"2105","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for him - meaning Anas. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in what You have provided him."
"2106","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month supplicating against Ril, Dhakwan and Lihyan."
"2107","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a garment of silk, and they began admiring it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A handkerchief - or he said: Some handkerchiefs - of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is softer than this, or better than this."
"2108","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"2109","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was in Paradise, I saw a river, so I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which your Lord has given you. So I put in my hand, and its soil was pungent musk."
"2110","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between the two sides of my Basin is like what is between Sanaa and Madinah, or like what is between Madinah and Amman."
"2111","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped at the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"2112","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perfect the bowing and prostration, for by Him in whose Hand is my soul, I surely see you from behind my back when you bow and prostrate."
"2113","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qurrah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: We awaited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Isha until half the night had passed. Then he came out and led us in prayer, as though I am looking at the glitter of his silver ring upon his hand."
"2114","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while making it complete."
"2115","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim plants a sapling - and once he said: or a palm - or sows a crop from which a beast, a human or a bird eats, except that it is charity for him."
"2116","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see a date, yet nothing prevents me from eating it except fear that it is from the dates of charity."
"2117","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing."
"2118","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying when he heard a man saying: Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise. When he finished his prayer he said: Which of you said such and such words? The people fell silent, until he said it three times. Then a man said: I said it, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended nothing but good. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw twelve angels racing to lift them up. Then the Blessed and Exalted said: Write them as My servant said, except that they asked their Lord how to write them. He said: Write them as My servant said."
"2119","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that some people of Uraynah came to Madinah and found its climate unsuitable. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered camels and their herdsman for them, and ordered them to drink from their milk and urine. He said: They grew fat until they were well-nourished, then they killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, and they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and cast them in the sun until they died."
"2120","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, Ali ibn Zayd and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no believer wish for death because of harm that has befallen him; if he must say something, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."
"2121","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"2122","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old while two traits grow young in him: greed for wealth, and desire for long life."
"2123","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"2124","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, deeds that are not raised, a heart that does not fear, and a supplication that is not heard."
"2125","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leprosy, madness, elephantiasis and evil diseases."
"2126","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym sent me with a basket containing fresh dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took handfuls sending them to his wives, then ate the remainder like one known to desire it."
"2127","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection and become anxious about that. They shall say: If only we sought intercession with our Lord Almighty so He relieves us from this place of ours. So they shall come to Adam, peace be upon him, and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind; Allah created you with His Hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things; intercede for us with our Lord so He relieves us from this place of ours. He shall say: I am not fit for that - and he shall mention to them the sin he committed - but go to Nuh, the first Messenger Allah sent to the earth. So they shall come to Nuh, and he shall say: I am not fit for that - and he shall mention to them the sin he committed - but go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Most Merciful, peace be upon him. So they shall come to Ibrahim, and he shall say: I am not fit for that - and he shall mention to them sins he committed - but go to Musa, peace be upon him, a servant to whom Allah gave the Torah and spoke to directly. So they shall come to Musa, peace be upon him, and he shall say: I am not fit for that - and he shall mention to them the sin he committed - but go to Isa, peace be upon him, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, His Word and His Spirit. So they shall come to Isa, and he shall say: I am not fit for that, but go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a servant whom Allah has forgiven his past and future sins. So they shall come to me, and I shall proceed and seek permission from my Lord, and permission shall be granted to me. When I see my Lord Blessed and Exalted I shall fall prostrate, and He shall leave me as long as He wills to leave me. Then it shall be said: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you shall be heard, ask and you shall be given, intercede and your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He teaches me, then I shall intercede, and a limit shall be set for me, and I shall admit them to Paradise. Then I shall return, and when I see my Lord I shall fall prostrate to Him, and He shall leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it shall be said: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you shall be heard, ask and you shall be given, intercede and your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He teaches me, then I shall intercede, and a limit shall be set for me, and I shall admit them to Paradise. Then I shall return, and when I see my Lord I shall fall prostrate to Him, and He shall leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it shall be said: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you shall be heard, ask and you shall be given, intercede and your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He teaches me, then I shall intercede, and a limit shall be set for me, and I shall admit them to Paradise. Until I return and say: O Lord, none remains in the Fire except those detained by the Quran - that is, those upon whom eternity is due."
"2128","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not wrong the believer for his good deed; he is rewarded with provision in this world for it, and recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is granted abundance in this world for it, but when the Day of Resurrection comes he shall have no good deed."
"2129","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer shall be given in Paradise the strength of so-and-so many women. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, can he bear that? He said: He shall be given the strength of a hundred."
"2130","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every person has three companions. One companion says: What you spend is yours, and what you withhold is not yours - that is his wealth. Another companion says: I am with you, but when you reach the gate of the king I leave you and return - those are his family and retinue. And another companion says: I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave - that is his deeds. Then he says: You were indeed the least of the three in my regard - or he said: in your regard."
"2131","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah; and from Abu Awanah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three men among those before you went out seeking pasture for their families, and rain befell them, so they took shelter in a mountain, and a rock fell upon them. One said to another: The trace has been effaced; you see the rock has fallen, and none knows your place but Allah, so supplicate to Allah with your firmest deeds. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel, and when I came to them while they were asleep, I stood waiting until they awoke whenever they awoke, disliking that their drowsiness stir in their heads; when they awoke they drank. If You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved. Another said: O Allah, if You know there was a woman who pleased me, but she refused to yield herself to me until I offered her a reward; when I took hold of her, I spared her person and her reward. If You know I did that only fearing Your punishment and hoping for Your mercy, relieve us. He said: So another third moved. The third said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a laborer to work for me a day, and he worked, and when night came I gave him his wage, but he scorned it and did not take it; so I took his wage and multiplied it for him until it became much wealth. Then he came to me seeking his wage, and I said: Take all this, it is yours; had I wished I would have given him only his wage. If You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. He said: So the last third moved, and they walked out."
"2132","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah cauterized me while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, and I was not forbidden from it."
"2133","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, supplicating against a clan of the Arab clans, then abandoned it."
"2134","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man drinking while standing. I said to Anas: What do you say about eating while standing? He said: It is worse."
"2135","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas saying: Four gathered the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu Zayd. He said: I said to Anas: Who is Abu Zayd? He said: One of my uncles."
"2136","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with people who raise their eyes in prayer? His speech about that grew stern until he said: They shall certainly stop that, or their sight shall surely be snatched away."
"2137","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man used to write for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he dictated to him: All-Hearing, All-Seeing, he wrote: All-Hearing, All-Knowing; and when it was: All-Hearing, All-Knowing, he wrote: All-Hearing, All-Seeing. He had recited al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and whoever recited them had recited much of the Quran. He said: The man turned Christian and said: I used to write whatever I wished in the presence of Muhammad. He said: He died and was buried, but the earth cast him out; then he was buried and the earth cast him out. Anas said: Abu Talhah said: I saw him cast upon the surface of the earth."
"2138","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out to us after the call for Maghrib while we were praying two rakahs, and he neither commanded us nor forbade us."
"2139","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: That upon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah was something worth ten dirhams."
"2140","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my nation is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"2141","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty fashioned Adam, peace be upon him, He left him as long as He willed to leave him. Iblis began circling him looking at him, and when he saw him hollow he knew he was a creation without self-control."
"2142","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the bravest of people."
"2143","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam - or Uthman - narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Intercession is for the people of major sins among my nation."
"2144","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us when there were only I, my mother and my maternal aunt Umm Haram. He said: Stand, I shall pray with you. So he prayed with us outside the prayer time. A man said to Thabit: Where did he place Anas? He said: He placed him to his right. When he finished his prayer he supplicated for us - the household - for every good of this world and the Hereafter. My mother said: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant; supplicate to Allah for him. He said: So he supplicated for me for every good, and among the last of what he supplicated for me was: O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him therein. Abu Dawud said: They mentioned that Anas said: Eighty were born of my loins."
"2145","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is called, do not stand until you see me."
"2146","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: My cousin Harithah went out on the day of Badr as a young onlooker; he did not go out to fight, and an arrow struck and killed him. His mother came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if Harithah is in Paradise I shall be patient, and if otherwise you shall see what I do. He said: O mother of Harithah, there are many gardens, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaws."
"2147","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never prayed behind anyone lighter in prayer than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while making it complete. The prayer of Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, was close to it; when it was Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, he lengthened Fajr."
"2148","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas brought out a cup for us and said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink in this: water, honey, milk and date-drink."
"2149","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day I served him, and when I finished my service and returned intending my mother, I saw boys playing, so I stood watching their play. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them, greeted them, then called me and sent me on an errand of his, and sat in the shade until I came to him, and I was delayed from my mother beyond the time I used to come to her. She said: My son, what detained you? I told her. She said: What is this he sent you for? I said: Mother, it is the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: My son, then guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I never told it to anyone among people; had I told anyone I would have told you, O Thabit."
"2150","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: We were with Anas when he said: By Allah, I do not recognize today anything I knew in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: O Abu Hamzah, what of prayer? He said: Have you not introduced into prayer what you have introduced?"
"2151","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raid at dawn, listening; if he heard the adhan he held back, otherwise he raided."
"2152","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abbad ibn Bishr al-Ansari and Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ansari went out to prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a pitch-dark night, meaning very dark. When they returned to their homes, a light appeared before them, until when they were about to part, a light accompanied each of them."
"2153","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate often, saying: O Allah, our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shubah said: I mentioned that to Qatadah, and he said: Anas used to supplicate with it, but did not attribute it to the Prophet."
"2154","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until it was said: He is fasting, fasting; and break fast until it was said: He has broken fast, broken fast."
"2155","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, send with us Muadh ibn Jabal to teach us the Book of our Lord and the practice of our Prophet. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and said: This is the trustee of this nation, and he sent him with them."
"2156","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: He used to describe to us the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When he raised his head from bowing he stood so long out of the length of standing that we would say: He has forgotten."
"2157","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Patience is at the first shock."
"2158","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who frequent the mosques of Allah are the people of Allah Almighty."
"2159","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek out perfume in the women's quarters."
"2160","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be spoken to on Friday after descending from the minbar."
"2161","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Women used to enter carrying waterskins on the day of Uhud."
"2162","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: My maternal uncle Anas ibn al-Nadr came - after whom I was named. He had not witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that weighed heavily upon him. He said: The first battle the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) witnessed, I was absent from it. By Allah, if Allah shows me a battle hereafter, Allah shall surely see what I do. He said: He feared to say more than that. When Uhud came the following year, he witnessed it, and saw Sad ibn Muadh retreating. He said: Where to, O Abu Amr? Ah, the scent of Paradise - I find it beyond Uhud. So he fought until he was killed, and over eighty wounds were found upon him, of sword-strokes, spear-thrusts and arrow-shots. His sister al-Rubayyi bint al-Nadr said: By Allah, I recognized my brother only by his fingertips, for he had handsome fingertips. He said: This verse was revealed: Among the believers are men who proved true what they pledged to Allah, to the end of the verse. Anas said: We used to think it was revealed concerning him."
"2163","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew deathly ill, Fatimah said: O my distress. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be no distress upon your father after today."
"2164","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Zadhadhan narrated to us, he said: We were with Thabit, and an elder was with him, when we mentioned what is recited in the two Eids. The elder said: I accompanied Anas ibn Malik to al-Zawiyah on a feast day, and a freedman of his was leading them in prayer. He recited: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: By the night when it covers. So Anas said: He has recited the two chapters with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the Eid."
"2165","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits was seen. Shubah said: I mentioned that to Ali ibn Zayd, and he said: That is only in seeking rain. I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to Allah."
"2166","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Anjashah used to chant for the women, and al-Bara ibn Malik used to chant for the men. Anjashah had a beautiful voice, and when he chanted the camels quickened their pace. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you, O Anjashah; gently drive the glass vessels."
"2167","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the illness in which he passed away, and he said: Convey peace to your people, for they are chaste and patient."
"2168","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first thing that shall gather people is a Fire gathering them from the east to the west."
"2169","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first thing the people of Paradise shall eat is the extra lobe of the fish liver."
"2170","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When a Jewish woman menstruated, they would not eat with her, drink with her, nor stay with her in the house. So Allah Almighty revealed: And they ask you about menstruation; say: It is harm, up to His saying: until they are pure. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that they eat with them, drink with them, stay with them in houses, and do whatever they wished except intercourse. The Jews said: This man intends to leave nothing of our practice but oppose us in it. Then Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr came and mentioned that remark of the Jews to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not have intercourse with them? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed color until we thought he was angry with them. They left him, then a gift of milk came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sent after them until he gave them milk to drink; so we thought he was not angry with them."
"2171","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two men love one another for the sake of Allah Almighty except that the better of them is the one with stronger love for his companion."
"2172","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) purchased Safiyyah for seven heads."
"2173","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, Hammad ibn Salamah and Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us - all of them - from Thabit, from Anas. Abu Dawud said: And a shaykh who heard it from al-Nadr ibn Anas narrated it to us - and the narration of some of them entered into that of others. He said: Malik, the father of Anas, said to his wife Umm Sulaym - who is the mother of Anas: This man - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - forbids wine. So he set out until he reached Syria and perished there. Then Abu Talhah came and proposed to Umm Sulaym, speaking to her about that. She said: O Abu Talhah, one like you is not refused, but you are a disbelieving man while I am a Muslim woman; it is not lawful for me to marry you. He said: That is not your wont. She said: What is my wont? He said: Yellow and white wealth. She said: I want neither yellow nor white; I want Islam from you. He said: Who shall arrange that for me? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shall arrange that for you. So Abu Talhah set out intending the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions. When he saw him he said: Abu Talhah has come to you, with the brightness of Islam between his eyes. So he came and told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what Umm Sulaym had said, and he married her upon that. Thabit said: We never heard of a dowry greater than it, for she accepted Islam as dowry. So he married her; she was a woman with beautiful eyes, with some youthfulness. She stayed with him until a son was born to him, whom Abu Talhah loved dearly. The boy fell ill, and Abu Talhah was humbled by his illness - or weakened on his account. Abu Talhah went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the boy died. Umm Sulaym said: Let none announce the death of his son to Abu Talhah until I am the one to announce it to him. So she prepared the boy and laid him down. Abu Talhah came from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered upon her. He said: How is my son? She said: O Abu Talhah, he has never been calmer since his complaint than at this hour. He said: Praise belongs to Allah. So she brought him his supper and he ate from it. Then she perfumed herself and presented herself to him, and he had intercourse with her. When she knew he had eaten and had intercourse with her, she said: O Abu Talhah, tell me: if some people lent others a loaned object of theirs, then asked for it back, would they have the right to withhold it? He said: No. She said: Allah Almighty had lent you your son as a loan, then took him back to Himself, so reckon your son as lost and be patient. He grew angry, then said: You left me until after I had done what I did, then you announced my son to me. Then he went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you both in what passed of your night. So she conceived from that. Umm Sulaym used to travel with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she would go out with him when he went out and enter with him when he entered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When she gives birth, bring me the boy. Labor seized her on the night they neared Madinah, and she said: O Allah, I used to enter when Your Prophet entered and go out when Your Prophet went out, and this matter has come. So she gave birth to a boy, and said to her son Anas: Take the boy to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Anas took the boy to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was branding camels or sheep. When he looked at him he said to Anas: Has the daughter of Milhan given birth? He said: Yes. So he threw down what was in his hand, took the boy, and said: Bring me some Ajwah dates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the dates and began to chew them for the boy, while the boy smacked his lips. He said: Look at the love of the Ansar for dates. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chewed dates for him and named him Abdullah. Thabit said: He was counted among the best of the Muslims."
"2174","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the king of Rome gifted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a tunic of fine silk. He wore it, and I can almost see his nipples moving beneath it. His Companions began touching it and saying: This has been sent down to you from heaven. He said: What do you admire in it? By Him in whose Hand is my soul, a handkerchief of the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is softer than this. Then he sent it to Jafar, who wore it and came. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not give it to you to wear. He said: What shall I do with it? He said: Send it to your brother, the Negus."
"2175","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you wish for death; if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."
"2176","2171 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pass by the door of Fatimah for a month before the dawn prayer, saying: ""The prayer, O people of the house: {Allah only intends to remove defilement from you, O people of the house}."""
"2177","2172 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When I was taken on the Night Journey, I came upon people whose lips were being cut off with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the preachers from your ummah."""
"2178","2173 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, he said: I heard Anas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."""
"2179","2174 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let none of you wish for death because of some harm that has befallen him; but if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me in death when death is better for me."""
"2180","2175 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, he said: They passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a funeral, and they praised him with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become due."" And they passed by with another funeral and spoke evil of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become due."" Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, what has become due? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You are the witnesses of Allah on earth; whomever you praise with good, Paradise has become due for him, and whomever you speak of with evil, the Fire has become due for him."""
"2181","2176 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man perfume himself with saffron."
"2182","2177 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz or Thabit - Abu Dawud was in doubt - from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out to the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and none of them would undo his habwah except Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both; he would smile at them and they would smile at him."
"2183","2178 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Anas, he said: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said tashmit for one of them but did not say it for the other. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you said tashmit for this one but did not say it for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He praised Allah, so I said tashmit for him, but you did not praise Allah, so I did not say it for you."""
"2184","2179 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: We startled a rabbit at Marr al-Zahran, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran after it and grew tired, but I caught up with it and slaughtered it with a sharp stone. I brought it to Abu Talhah, and he sent a thigh of it - or its two hind legs - to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ate it. I said: Did he eat it? He said: He accepted it."
"2185","2180 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Zayd informed me, from Anas, that a woman of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to speak to him about something, and she was alone with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are indeed the most beloved of people to me"" - meaning the Ansar."
"2186","2181 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the Hour comes while a palm shoot is in the hand of one of you, then if he is able not to let the Hour come until he plants it, let him do so."""
"2187","2182 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, that a man of the People of the Book greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Al-sam be upon you."" Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."""
"2188","2183 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up animals alive as targets."
"2189","2184 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Anas informed me, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."""
"2190","2185 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I asked Musa ibn Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reach the point of needing to dye, but Abu Bakr used to dye with henna and katam."
"2191","2186 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has entrusted an angel with the womb, and he says: O Lord, a drop; O Lord, a clot; O Lord, a lump of flesh. Then when Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, intends to complete its creation, he says: O Lord, male or female, wretched or blessed? And that is written while it is in its mother's womb."""
"2192","2187 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas, that a man peeped at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his rooms, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a barbed arrowhead with him. Anas said: I saw him stealthily moving it to stab him with it."
"2193","2188 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the major sins, and he said: ""Associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, killing a soul, and false testimony"" - or ""false speech."""
"2194","2189 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm, he said: I heard Anas, when he was asked about the takbir in prayer when bowing and prostrating, say: He says takbir when he bows, when he rises, when he prostrates, and when he stands from the two rak'ahs. He said: From whom? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Abu Bakr, and from Umar. Hakim said to him: And from Uthman? He said: And from Uthman."
"2195","2190 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a garment of sundus silk to Umar. Umar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent this to me although you said what you said - meaning about silk. He said: ""I did not send it to you to wear it, but so that you may benefit from it or enjoy its value."""
"2196","2191 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter the house of Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed when she was not there. One day she was told: Here is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on your bed. She came to him while he had sweated profusely, as it was hot, so she took a bottle and began collecting some of that sweat into the bottle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: ""What are you doing?"" She said: O Messenger of Allah, your blessing; we put it in our perfume. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have done right."""
"2197","2192 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Anas, he said: Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn outnumbering the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their women, children, camels, and sheep, and the Muslims were routed that day. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day kept saying: O Hawazin; O company of Muslims, Muhajirun and Ansar, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; O company of Muslims, come to me, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then Allah routed the polytheists without a spear being thrust or an arrow shot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: ""Whoever kills a polytheist, his spoils belong to him."" Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, I charged at a man and struck him on the cord of the shoulder, but I was turned away from him, and he wore a coat of mail; see who took it. A man said: I took it, O Messenger of Allah; give it to me and compensate him from it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never used to be asked for anything but he gave it, or remained silent. Umar said: No, by Allah, Allah will not bestow it upon a lion of His lions and then we give it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Umar has spoken the truth."" Abu Talhah saw with Umm Sulaym a dagger and said: What are you doing with this? She said: I intend, if any of the polytheists draws near, to rip open his belly. Abu Talhah mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: ""O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well."" She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill these who flee with you."
"2198","2193 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Anas, he said: When this verse was revealed: {You will never attain righteousness} - the verse - Abu Talhah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I see that Allah is asking us for a loan, and I call you to witness that my land at Ariha is charity; let the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place it wherever he wishes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Place it among your relatives."" So he made it gardens shared between Hassan ibn Thabit and Ubayy ibn Ka'b."
"2199","2194 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever refuse perfume when it was offered to him."
"2200","2195 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas informed me, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among people there are people who are keys to good and locks against evil, and among people there are people who are keys to evil and locks against good. So glad tidings to one at whose hands the keys of good are placed, and woe to one at whose hands the keys of evil are placed."""
"2201","2196 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Attab, the freedman of Hurmuz, narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine to hear and obey as much as I am able."
"2202","2197 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Attab, he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"2203","2198 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah, Shu'bah, and Abd al-Warith narrated to us - the best of them in narrating it - all of them narrating to us from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, he stayed in its high part with a clan of the Ansar called Banu Amr ibn Awf, remaining among them fourteen nights. Then he sent for Banu al-Najjar, and they came to him with their swords slung. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his mount with Abu Bakr riding behind him. He went on until he stopped in the courtyard of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. He said: O Banu al-Najjar, set a price for me for this walled enclosure of yours. They said: No, by Allah, we will take no price for it except from Allah and from His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray wherever prayer overtook him, and would pray in sheepfolds. Anas said: In it was what I tell you: there were palm trees - Hammad said: and ploughed land, while Abd al-Warith said: ruins - and the graves of the polytheists. He ordered the palms cut down, the graves of the polytheists dug up, and the ruins levelled. He made the palms face the qiblah of the mosque. They began carrying stones and chanting, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them."
"2204","2199 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Make things easy and do not make them hard; give glad tidings of calm and do not repel people."""
"2205","2200 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah informed me, he said: I heard Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr: ""Hear and obey, even if it be an Abyssinian whose head is like a raisin."""
"2206","2201 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."""
"2207","2202 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mix with us so much that he would say to a little brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do?"
"2208","2203 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two"" - and he pointed with the forefinger and the middle finger."
"2209","2204 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was thrown from a horse and his right side was scraped. He prayed sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. When he gave the salutation he said: ""The imam is only appointed to be followed, so when he says takbir, say takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs all praise; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays sitting, pray all of you sitting."""
"2210","2205 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b, Zam'ah, and Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not sever ties, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."""
"2211","2206 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."""
"2212","2207 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr, and one going to al-Awali would go while the sun was still high."
"2213","2208 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in our house, so we milked a sheep for him and mixed it with water from the well. The cup was handed over, with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, on his left and a Bedouin on the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank and gave the Bedouin his remainder, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one on the right, then the one on the right."""
"2214","2209 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: Bilal was commanded to make the adhan even-numbered and the iqamah odd-numbered."
"2215","2210 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most merciful of my ummah to my ummah is Abu Bakr; the firmest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar; the most modest of them - or the truest of them in modesty - is Uthman; the most knowledgeable of them of the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal; the most knowledgeable of them of what Allah revealed to me is Ubayy ibn Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of them of the shares of inheritance is Zayd ibn Thabit; and the trustworthy one of this ummah is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."""
"2216","2211 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on a mat."
"2217","2212 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: A man said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? He said: I never saw him pray it."
"2218","2213 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked qunut for a month, supplicating against Usayyah."
"2219","2214 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: We asked Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that - mentioning the small amount of his white hair - but Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, dyed with henna and katam."
"2220","2215 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr informed me, he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Ansar: Love of the Ansar is a sign of the believer and a sign of the hypocrite; none loves them but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite."
"2221","2216 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabr informed me, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a makkuq and bathe with five makakiyy."
"2222","2217 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Durust narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Aban al-Raqashi, from Anas, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun and the moon are two castrated bulls in the Fire."""
"2223","2218 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For me to sit with people remembering Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, from the morning prayer until sunrise is dearer to me than that over which the sun rises; and for me to remember Allah from the Asr prayer until sunset is dearer to me than freeing eight of the descendants of Isma'il, the blood-money of each one of them being twelve thousand."" So we counted their blood-moneys in a sitting and they reached ninety-six thousand. Here there is one who says ""four of the descendants of Isma'il"" - but by Allah, he said nothing but ""eight, the blood-money of each one of them being twelve thousand."""
"2224","2219 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting six days of the year: the three days of Tashriq, the day of Fitr, the day of Adha, and Friday singled out among the days."
"2225","2220 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the call to prayer is made, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."" Yazid said: And it used to be said: ""Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."""
"2226","2221 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the people to fast a day and that none break his fast until he gave him permission. The people fasted, and in the evening a man would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have remained fasting since today; permit me to break my fast, and he would permit him. Then another man would come saying that, and he would permit him, until a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, two young women of your household have remained fasting since today; permit them to break their fast. He turned away from him, then he repeated it to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They did not fast; how can one have fasted who spent the day eating the flesh of people? Go and command them, if they are fasting, to vomit."" They did so, and each one of them vomited a clot. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had they died while it was still in them, the Fire would have consumed them."""
"2227","2222 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Straighten your rows and stand close together, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I see the devils among your rows as though they were dusty sheep."""
"2228","2223 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Wrongdoing is of three kinds: a wrong that Allah will not leave, a wrong that is forgiven, and a wrong that is not forgiven. As for the wrong that is not forgiven, it is shirk, which Allah does not forgive. As for the wrong that is forgiven, it is the servant's wrong between him and his Lord. As for that which is not left, it is Allah's settling of some of them from others."""
"2229","2224 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution on Friday, then with it - and what an excellent thing - and whoever bathes, then bathing is better."""
"2230","2225 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid, he said: We said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, what do you say about the children of the polytheists? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They had no evil deeds to be punished for and thus be of the people of the Fire, nor had they good deeds to be rewarded for and thus be kings of the people of Paradise; they are the servants of the people of Paradise."""
"2231","2226 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Durust narrated to us, from Yazid, from Anas, that a man was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that he had died. He said: ""The one who was with us just now?"" He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is as though a sudden seizure in anger, and the deprived one is he who is deprived of his bequest."""
"2232","2227 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Hafsah bint Sirin, she said: Anas said to me: Of what did Yahya ibn Abi Amrah die? I said: Of the plague. Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."""
"2233","2228 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Rib'i ibn Abdullah ibn al-Jarud al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from my grandfather al-Jarud, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when on a journey and wanting to pray voluntary prayer, would face the qiblah, say takbir, then pray wherever his mount turned with him."
"2234","2229 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was merciful toward dependents."
"2235","2230 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My grandfather al-Hilal ibn Ali narrated to me, from Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting at the edge of the grave of his daughter while she was being buried, and I saw his eyes shedding tears, and he had Abu Talhah descend into her grave."
"2236","2231 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution for every prayer? He said: Yes."
"2237","2232 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Asim [editorial note in the print: in the Dar Hajar edition it is thus, and the correct form is Abu Isam, as in the sources of takhrij], from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he drank, would breathe three times, and he said: It is more wholesome, more pleasant, and more healing. [Garbled print apparatus retained: the chain contains a noted scribal variant; translation literal.]"
"2238","2233 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freeing her dowry."
"2239","2234 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his household used to bathe from a single vessel."
"2240","2235 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Asma, from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Labbayk with Umrah and Hajj together."""
"2241","2236 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am mentioned in his presence, let him send blessings upon me; and whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah will send blessings upon him tenfold."""
"2242","2237 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah Sa'id ibn Yazid, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in sandals? He said: Yes."
"2243","2238 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl al-Uqayli narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has people who are His own among mankind."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: ""The people of the Qur'an; they are the people of Allah and His chosen ones."""
"2244","2239 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala al-Qutabi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in Zuhr prayer in winter, and we would not know whether more of the day had passed or more remained."
"2245","2240 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salm al-Alawi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not confront anyone to his face with anything; one day a man came to him wearing yellow perfume, and he said: ""If only you would command this one to wash off this yellowness from himself."""
"2246","2241 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to enter Khaybar, he said: ""Allah is Greatest; Khaybar is ruined; Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is conquered. Indeed when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned."""
"2247","2242 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Humayd informed me, he heard Anas saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married for the weight of a date-stone of gold, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."""
"2248","2243 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a slave boy of ours and cupped him, ordering for him a sa' or two sa's, or a mudd or two mudds; then intercession was made concerning him, so his tax was lightened."
"2249","2244 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of al-Huraqah, narrated to us, he said: I and Umar ibn Thabit entered upon Anas, after we had prayed Zuhr with Khalid ibn Asid. He said: Have you prayed Asr? We said: No, but we prayed Zuhr with Khalid. He said: Stand and pray Asr, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""That is the prayer of the hypocrite: he prays it close to sunset, remembering Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, in it but little; he leaves it until when it is at sunset, he stands and prays it, remembering Allah in it but little."""
"2250","2245 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: ""And what have you prepared for it?"" He said: I have not prepared for it much prayer, fasting, or charity, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then you are with those whom you love."""
"2251","2246 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from Abu al-Abyad, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was white and high."
"2252","2247 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The leaders are from Quraysh: when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfil, and when mercy is sought from them they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from them."""
"2253","2248 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go to relieve himself, and I and a boy of the Ansar would follow him with a small waterskin of water, and he would cleanse himself with it."
"2254","2249 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My Hawd is from such-and-such to such-and-such; in it are vessels as numerous as the stars, more fragrant than musk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, and whiter than milk. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst again, and whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched."" [Flag: endpoints left vague in the Arabic.]"
"2255","2250 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Sadaqah, the freedman of Anas, informed me, he said: I asked Anas about the times of prayer, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr between these two prayers of yours, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr from the rising of dawn until sight spreads out."
"2256","2251 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Habib narrated to us - Abu Dawud said: We never met among the companions of Anas one more trustworthy than him; Hammad ibn Zayd and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from him, and Shu'bah used to visit him - he said: I heard Anas saying, and he raised it: ""People will come out of the Fire after they have burned, and will enter Paradise."""
"2257","2252 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Anas and said to him: When did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Asr? He said: He used to pray it while the sun was white and clear."
"2258","2253 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman al-Khuza'i narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in Friday prayer when the sun declined."
"2259","2254 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas or al-Hasan - Abu Dawud was in doubt - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out leaning on Usamah ibn Zayd in the illness in which he died, and led the people in prayer in a single garment, a Qitri garment, with its ends crossed."
"2260","2255 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman and Sadaqah narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Anas, he said: A limit of forty days was set for us for trimming the nails, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpits, and trimming the mustache."
"2261","2256 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Mada'ini, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to seek refuge from eight: anxiety, grief, incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, the burden of debt, and the overpowering of men."
"2262","2257 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit and Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt, like for like"" - or he said: ""weight for weight."" One of them said, and the other did not say it: ""There is no harm in a dinar for silver, two for one, hand to hand; no harm in wheat for barley, two for one; and no harm in salt for barley, two for one, hand to hand."""
"2263","2258 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abu Fazarah narrating from Anas, he said: We used to pray the two rak'ahs - meaning before Maghrib - in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2264","2259 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Shumayt narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrating to my father and my uncle, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Begging is not lawful except for one of three: overwhelming debt, grinding poverty, or painful blood-money."""
"2265","2260 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Shumayt narrated to us, he said: My father and my uncle narrated to me, from Abu Bakr, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold by auction a cloak and a cup, saying: ""Who will buy?"" A man said: For a dirham. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who will bid more?"""
"2266","2261 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Rib'i ibn Abdullah ibn al-Jarud al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: al-Jarud narrated to me, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit my mother Umm Sulaym and she would present him with something. One day he visited us while a little brother of mine was with her, and he saw him heavy-spirited. He said: ""What is wrong with your son, O Umm Sulaym?"" She said: O Messenger of Allah, his little bird that he used to play with has died. He said: ""O Abu Umayr, the nughayr has died; time has overtaken it."""
"2267","2262 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muslim Abu Abdullah al-A'war narrated to me, he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ride the donkey, wear wool, answer the invitation of the slave, and I saw him on the day of Khaybar on a donkey whose bridle was of palm fibre."
"2268","2263 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Anas pray over a man, standing at the head of the bier; then a woman of Quraysh was brought and he prayed over her, standing near the middle of the bier. Among those who attended his funeral was al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi. When he saw the difference in his standing we said: O Abu Hamzah, is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand for a woman and a man as you stood? He said: Yes. Then he turned to us and said: Remember this."
"2269","2264 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: I came to Umar after the death of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Raise your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you upon what I pledged to your two companions before you - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr - so I pledged allegiance to him to hear and obey as much as I am able."
"2270","2265 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Let neither fear of people"" - or ""awe of people,"" Shu'bah said one of the two - ""prevent any one of you from speaking a truth he knows."" And matters kept being forgotten until we fell short."
"2271","2266 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When there are three on a journey, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the best reciter among them."""
"2272","2267 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil Bashir ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, that a Bedouin asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I am in a garden full of lizards, and it is the main food of my family? He remained silent. We said: Ask him again. He asked again and he remained silent. Then we said: Ask him again. He asked a third time, and he said: ""O Bedouin, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, was angry with two tribes of the Children of Israel and transformed them into beasts crawling on the earth, and I do not know whether these are some of them; I neither forbid you from them nor command you to eat them."""
"2273","2268 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Na'amah al-Sa'di narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his sandals, and the people prayed in their sandals; then he took off his sandals, and the people took off their sandals while in prayer. When he finished his prayer he said: ""What made you take off your sandals in prayer?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do it so we did it. He said: ""Jibril informed me that there was filth in them; so when one of you comes to the mosque, let him look: if he sees filth in his sandals, otherwise let him pray in them."""
"2274","2269 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Tarif ibn Sufyan, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we came to a pond in which there was carrion. Some of the people performed ablution, and some refrained until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came at the rear of the people and said: ""Perform ablution and drink, for nothing makes water impure."""
"2275","2270 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered to us a sermon after Asr until sunset; whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. He said: ""Verily this world is green and sweet, and Allah is making you stewards over it, watching how you act. So beware of this world and beware of women. Verily the children of Adam were created in various ranks: among them is one born a believer, living a believer, and dying a believer; among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a disbeliever; among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a believer; and among them is one born a believer, living a believer, and dying a disbeliever. Verily the best of traders is he who is good in settling debts and good in seeking them, and the worst of traders is he who is bad in settling and bad in seeking; but if he is good in settling and bad in seeking, or good in seeking and bad in settling, then it is offset by that. Verily the worst of men is he who is quick to anger and slow to calm, and the best of men is he who is slow to anger and quick to calm; but if he is quick to anger and quick to calm, then it is offset by that, and if he is slow to anger and slow to calm, then it is offset by that. Verily anger is a live coal kindled in the belly of the son of Adam - have you not seen the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his veins? When that happens, then to the ground, to the ground. Verily every traitor will have a banner according to his treachery."" Al-Hasan said: It will be set up at his backside. Then he returned to the hadith of Abu Sa'id and said: ""And no traitor is greater in treachery than a leader of the generality. Let not awe of people prevent a man from speaking the truth when he knows it. Verily there remains of this world, of what has passed of it, only like what remains of this day of yours of what has passed of it."""
"2276","2271 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn when eighteen nights of Ramadan had passed; groups of people fasted and others broke their fast, and neither blamed the fasting one for his fast nor the one breaking fast for breaking it."
"2277","2272 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon: ""Let not fear of people prevent a man from speaking the truth when he knows it."""
"2278","2273 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2279","2274 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mustamirr narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of perfume is musk."""
"2280","2275 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that he was struck by hunger - or a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was struck by hunger - and some of his household said to him: If only you would go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he would give you something. He went and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, saying: ""Whoever seeks independence, Allah will enrich him; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; and whoever asks us and we find something, we will give him."" So he returned and did not ask him, nor did he ask anyone after that."
"2281","2276 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some lagging among his Companions, so he said: Follow me, and let those after you follow you; people will keep lagging until Allah puts them behind."
"2282","2277 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr before dawn."
"2283","2278 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that al-Ash'ari sought permission to enter upon Umar but he did not permit him, so he returned. He sent to him: What turned you back? He said: I sought permission three times and was not permitted, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one seeking permission seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return. He said: You shall bring me one who knows this, or I shall do such-and-such to you. Abu Sa'id said: Al-Ash'ari came to me trembling, his face pale, and stood before a circle of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I adjure by Allah any man who knows anything of this but to stand and testify to it, for I have feared this man for myself. Abu Sa'id said: I said: I am with you. Another said: And I am with you. So he was relieved."
"2284","2279 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A division will occur between two parties of my ummah; a renegade group will break away between them, and the party nearer to the truth of the two will kill them."
"2285","2280 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it with seven nights remaining, or five remaining, or three remaining."
"2286","2281 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-fourth."""
"2287","2282 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug the Trench, the people would carry brick by brick, while Ammar was unwell from an ailment he had, so he began carrying two bricks at a time. Abu Sa'id said: My companions narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would shake the dust from his head, saying: ""Woe to you, son of Sumayyah; the rebellious party will kill you."""
"2288","2283 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Ja'far, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of perfume is musk."""
"2289","2284 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id said to Ibn Abbas: What do you think of your fatwa about exchange - is it something you say by your own opinion or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: No, but I see no harm in it when it is hand to hand. Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was brought dates better than the dates usually brought to him. He said: ""From where is this?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I went to the household of so-and-so, gave them two sa's and took one sa'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Return their sa' to them and bring us our two sa's."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt, like for like"" - or he said: ""equal for equal"" - ""whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury."""
"2290","2285 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Harb al-Nadbi narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade garlic, onions, and leeks. We said: O Abu Sa'id, is it unlawful? He said: No."
"2291","2286 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam, naqir, and muzaffat vessels. We said: O Abu Sa'id, is it unlawful? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"2292","2287 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal fasting, yet this sister of mine fasts continuously and I forbid her."
"2293","2288 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated at Arafat, holding his hands thus: placing their backs toward heaven and their palms toward the earth."
"2294","2289 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu al-Waddak narrating from Abu Sa'id, he said: When we captured the captives of Khaybar, we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus. He said: ""Not from all fluid does a child come; and when Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, intends to create something, nothing can prevent Him."""
"2295","2290 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Abu al-Waddak saying: I will not drink from a dubba after I heard Abu Sa'id saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunk man. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not drink wine; I drank from a dubba. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning him, so he was struck with sandals and pushed with hands, and he forbade making nabidh in dubba vessels."
"2296","2291 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin informed me, from Ma'bad ibn Sirin, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus, and he said: ""It is no harm upon you not to do it, for it is only decree."""
"2297","2292 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will follow the ways of those before you, so much so that if they entered the hole of a lizard, you would enter it."" It was said: Who are they? He said: ""The Jews and the Christians."""
"2298","2293 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam, the freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that some people said in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suffer any harm - Abu Dawud said: meaning, do you doubt - in seeing the sun at midday on a clear day with no clouds in it? They said: No. He said: Do you suffer any harm in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon on a clear night with no clouds in it? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You will suffer no more harm in seeing Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection than in seeing either of them. When it is the Day of Resurrection, a caller will call: Every nation followed what it used to worship, and none remains who used to worship other than Allah, of idols and divining arrows, but they will fall into the Fire, until none remains except those who worshipped Allah, righteous or wicked, and the remnants of the People of the Book. It will be said: What did you worship? They will say: We worshipped Uzayr the son of Allah. It will be said: You have lied; Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has taken neither wife nor son. What do you seek? They will say: Our Lord, we are thirsty, give us to drink. They will be motioned to: Will you not come to water? Hell will be raised before them as though a mirage, its parts crushing one another, until they fall into the Fire. Then the Christians will be called and it will be said to them: What did you worship? They will say: We worshipped the Messiah the son of Allah. It will be said: You have lied; Allah has taken neither wife nor son. What do you seek? They will say: Our Lord, we are thirsty, give us to drink. They will be motioned to: Will you not come to water? Hell will be raised before them as though a mirage, its parts crushing one another, until they fall into the Fire, until none remains except those who worshipped Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, righteous or wicked. The Lord of the worlds will come to them and say: What are you waiting for? Every nation has followed what it used to worship. They will say: We parted from people in this world and did not keep their company; we are waiting for our Lord whom we worshipped. He will say: Is there between you and your Lord a sign by which you know Him? They will say: Yes. Then the shin will be uncovered, and none remains who used to prostrate to Allah willingly in this world but he will be permitted to prostrate, and none remains who used to prostrate for show or hypocrisy but his back will become a single slab; whenever he tries to prostrate he will fall on his back. He said: Then they will raise their heads and He will say: I am your Lord. They will say: You are our Lord. The bridge will be laid and intercession permitted, and he will say: My Lord, grant safety, grant safety. The believers will pass over the bridge. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the bridge? He said: Slippery and sliding, and on it are hooks, clamps, and a flattened thorn with a hooked thorn called al-sa'dan. The believers will pass like the blink of an eye, like lightning, like wind, like fine horses and mounts: one saved and secure, one scratched and released, one heaped into the Fire. When the believers escape the Fire, then by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are not more insistent in asking me for the truth than the believers in Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, pleading for their brothers in the Fire. They will say: Our Lord, our brothers who used to pray with us, fast with us, and perform Hajj with us. He will say: Go, and whomever you recognize by his face, bring him out. Their images will be made forbidden to the Fire. They will go and bring them out, the Fire having taken a man up to his ankles and up to the middle of his shins. They will bring out a great multitude, then return and say: Our Lord, we have left in the Fire none of those whom You commanded us to bring out. He will say: Return, and whomever you find in his heart a dinar's weight of good, bring him out. They will go and bring out a great multitude, then return and say: We have left in the Fire none of those whom You commanded us to bring out. He will say: Return, and whomever you find in his heart half a mithqal of good, bring him out. They will return and bring out a great multitude, then return and say: We have left in the Fire none of those whom You commanded us to bring out except we brought him out. He will say: Return, and whomever you find in his heart an atom's weight of good, bring him out. They will go and bring out a great multitude, then return and say: We have left in the Fire none of those whom You commanded us to bring out except we brought him out - and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri used to say: If you do not believe this hadith, then recite this verse: {Indeed Allah does not wrong even an atom's weight} - the verse - then He, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded, and none remains but the Most Merciful of the merciful. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will take a handful from the Fire and bring out of it people who never did any good at all, having become charred. They will be cast into a river at the mouths of Paradise called the River of Life. They will come out of their decayed state as a seed comes out of flood-borne debris - have you not seen how what is toward the tree and the stone is green or yellow, and what of it is in the shade is white? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as though you used to graze in the desert! They will come out like pearls, with seals on their necks. It will be said: These are the freed ones of Allah, brought out of the Fire without any deed they did nor any good they sent forth. It will be said: Enter Paradise; whatever you see of anything is yours. They will say: Our Lord, You have given us what You gave none of the worlds. He will say: You have with Me what is better than this? They will say: O Lord, what is better than this? He will say: My pleasure; I shall never be angry with you after it."
"2299","2294 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat on the minbar and we sat around him. He said: ""What I fear for you after me is what will be opened for you of the bloom and adornment of this world."" A man said: Does good bring evil? He remained silent. It was said to him: What is wrong with you, speaking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he does not speak to you? We saw that revelation was descending upon him. Then he recovered and wiped the sweat from himself, saying: ""Where is the questioner?"" - as though praising him - and said: ""Good does not bring evil. Among what spring produces, some kills by overeating or nearly does, except the eater of green fodder: it eats until its flanks are full, then faces the sun, urinates, defecates, ruminates. This wealth is green and sweet, and how excellent is the wealth of the Muslim for one who gives from it to the poor, the orphan, and the wayfarer"" - or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - ""and whoever takes it without right is like one who eats and is never satisfied, and it will bear witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2300","2295 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not sell silver for silver except like for like."""
"2301","2296 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar."""
"2302","2297 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not revile my Companions, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it."""
"2303","2298 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a funeral, let him stand; and whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is laid down."""
"2304","2299 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dhakwan Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man of the Ansar and sent for him. He came out with his head dripping. He said: ""Perhaps we hurried you."" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you are hurried or deprived, there is no bath upon you, but ablution is upon you."""
"2305","2300 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Safwan, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, Allah will distance his face from Hell by seventy autumns."""
"2306","2301 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: We mentioned Laylat al-Qadr among a group of Quraysh, so I went to Abu Sa'id, who was a friend of mine. He said: Will you not go out with us to the palm groves? We went out while he wore a khamisah of his. I said: Inform me about Laylat al-Qadr; did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Yes. We observed i'tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the last ten of Ramadan. He addressed us on the morning of the twentieth, saying: I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, but I was made to forget it - or I forgot it - so seek it in the last ten, in the odd nights. Whoever observed i'tikaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him return. And I saw as though I were prostrating in water and mud. He said: We returned and saw no wisp of cloud in the sky, then a cloud came and we were rained upon until the roof of the mosque flowed, for it was of palm stalks. Prayer was established, and I saw him prostrating in water and mud, until I saw the mud on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or he said: the trace of mud on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2307","2302 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, he said: One who saw Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, when he was brought tharid and a lump, and a fly came and fell into it. Abu Salamah took it and dipped it into it. I said: What is this? He said: Abu Sa'id narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the vessel or drink of one of you, let him dip it into it, for one of its wings carries poison"" - or ""disease"" - ""and the other carries cure; it raises the cure and lays down the disease."""
"2308","2303 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We used to be given mixed dates as provision in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would give two sa's for one sa'. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Verily no two sa's of dates for one sa', no two sa's of wheat for one sa', and no two dirhams for one dirham."""
"2309","2304 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you see a funeral, stand; and whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is laid down."""
"2310","2305 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihzam narrated to us: Umarah al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: We used to visit Abu Sa'id, and when he saw us he would say: Welcome to the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: ""There will come people seeking knowledge; when you see them, treat them kindly."""
"2311","2306 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever reaches dawn without having prayed witr, there is no witr for him."""
"2312","2307 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Umarah al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id, he said: Coitus interruptus was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""If Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, decrees something, it will surely be, even with withdrawal."" Abu Sa'id said: I practised withdrawal with a slave girl of mine, and she gave birth to the dearest of people to me - this boy."
"2313","2308 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Firas al-Mukattib, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Charity is lawful for the rich when it is in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"2314","2309 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, that a slain man was found between two quarters. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that it be measured to which of the two he was nearer, and he was found nearer to one of the two quarters by a span. Abu Sa'id said: It is as though I am looking at the span of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he cast its blood-money upon them."
"2315","2310 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Muslim informed me, he said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab saying: Marwan put the sermon before the prayer, and a man stood and said: You have opposed the Sunnah; the sermon used to be after the prayer. He said: That has been left, O Abu so-and-so - Shu'bah said: he was ungrammatical - then Abu Sa'id stood and said: Who is this speaker? He has discharged his duty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: ""Whoever of you sees a wrong, let him denounce it with his hand; whoever cannot, let him denounce it with his tongue; whoever cannot, let him denounce it with his heart - and that is the weakest of faith."""
"2316","2311 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no charity on less than five awaqiyy, no charity on less than five awsuq, and no charity on less than five dhawd."""
"2317","2312 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he gave the salutation at the end of prayer, would say three times: ""Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and all praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."""
"2318","2313 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the well of Buda'ah, into which menstrual cloths and carrion are thrown? He said: ""Nothing makes water impure."""
"2319","2314 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id, he said: We used to sell ummahat al-awlad in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2320","2315 - Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Abu Sa'id, he said: When a man grew heavy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was attended, we would call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be with him. Sometimes that would be prolonged, so we said: This is hard upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we thought to leave him until he dies, then call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to him. We acted thus, then we thought it kinder to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to carry our biers to him. So we did, and such was the practice."
"2321","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Hisham, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"2322","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'a al-Zuraqi, from Abu Sa'id, who said: A man prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, then a man said: I am fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother prepared food and invited you, so break your fast and make up a day in its place."
"2323","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl and said: Let one out of every two men go forth, and the reward is shared between them."
"2324","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, he heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Abu Sa'id, who said: When this verse was revealed, {When the help of Allah comes and the victory}, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it until he completed it, then said: I and my Companions are one party, and the people are another party; there is no emigration after the conquest. Abu Sa'id said: I narrated this hadith to Marwan ibn al-Hakam when he was governor of Madinah, and he said: You have lied. With him were Zayd ibn Thabit and Rafi' ibn Khadij, and they were with him on the couch. Abu Sa'id said: If these two wished they could tell you, but this one fears he will strip him of the headship of his people, and this one fears he will strip him of the charity, meaning Zayd ibn Thabit. He said: So he raised the stick at him, and when they saw that they said: He has spoken the truth."
"2325","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from a man, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should belittle himself by seeing a matter concerning Allah about which he should speak, then failing to speak of it, so that he meets Allah, mighty and majestic, having neglected it, and He says: What prevented you? He says: Fear of people. He says: It was Me you were more deserving to fear."
"2326","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: There is no harm if you do not do it, for it is only the decree."
"2327","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sadaqa ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Ghalib al-Huddani, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits never combine in a believer: miserliness and bad character."
"2328","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Sahba, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Sa'id - Hammad said: I know it only as raised to the Prophet - who said: The limbs expiate for the tongue, saying: Fear Allah concerning us, for if you are upright we are upright, and if you deviate we deviate."
"2329","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, the freedman of al-Huraqa, who said: My father said to me: I have a need of you, and I thought he wanted something of the goods of this world. I said: O father, ask whatever you wish. He said: I ask you to come early to Friday prayer, for I heard Abu Sa'id say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels on Friday write down the people; like one who offers a camel, like one who brings forward a cow, like one who brings forward a sheep, like one who brings forward a bird, and like one who brings forward an egg. Then when the imam sits on the minbar the scrolls are folded."
"2330","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Hamza informed me, saying: I heard Hilal ibn Hisn say: I came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Sa'id in his house, and a gathering brought him and me together, and I heard him narrating. He said: I suffered hunger in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until I tied a stone over my stomach. My wife said to me: If you went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, for so-and-so came to him and asked him and he gave him, and so-and-so came to him and asked him and he gave him. I said: I will not ask him until I find nothing. So I searched and found nothing, then I set out to him and found him preaching, and I caught from his words: Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will enrich him. Whoever asks us, we will either give him or console him, and whoever feels no need of us is dearer to us than one who asks us. So I returned and never asked anyone for anything after that, then worldly wealth came to us, and no household among the Ansar had more wealth than us."
"2331","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Siddiq narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in the darkness of the night of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"2332","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywa ibn Shurayh al-Shami, from a man he named, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let none eat your food but a God-fearing person, and accompany none but a believer."
"2333","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you hear the caller calling to prayer, say the like of what he says."
"2334","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I heard Abu al-Mutawakkil narrating from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you intends to repeat it, let him perform ablution."
"2335","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir informed me, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghusl on Friday is obligatory, and that one touch perfume, and use the siwak. As for ghusl, I testify that it is obligatory; as for using the siwak and perfume, Allah knows whether they are obligatory or not, but this is what he said."
"2336","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Dawud al-Sarraj, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise will wear it but he will not wear it."
"2337","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Rayyan dates, while the dates of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Ba'l, meaning dry. He said to his servant: Where did you get this? He said: We sold two sa' of dates for one sa' of this. He said: Do not do that; sell your dates, then buy what you need of this."
"2338","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst thief among people is the one who steals from his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration."
"2339","Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-hantam, al-naqir, and al-muzaffat."
"2340","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamza ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Why do some people claim that my kinship will not benefit? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my kinship is joined in this world and the Hereafter. I am your forerunner, O people, at the Hawd. Peoples will come on the Day of Resurrection, and a speaker among them will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. I will say: As for lineage, I know it, but you apostatized after me and turned back on your heels."
"2341","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Utba narrating from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we recognized it in his face."
"2342","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, who heard Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrating from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers who oppress and lie; flatterers from among the people will come to them - Imran said: seekers of favor from among the people, and Shu'ba said: entrants from among the people - so whoever believes them in their lies is not of me and I am not of him."
"2343","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ibrahim al-Ansari, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions shaved their heads on the day of Hudaybiya except Uthman ibn Affan and Abu Qatada, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for those who shaved three times and for those who shortened once."
"2344","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like."
"2345","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Iyad, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We used to give the charity of Fitr in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sa' a sa', though their food in those days was dates and raisins."
"2346","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qibla of the mosque and scraped it off with a pebble, and said: A man should not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left or under his foot."
"2347","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of al-Huraqa, from his father, who said: I asked Abu Sa'id about the lower garment, and he said: You have come upon one well informed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer - or he said: of the Muslim - is to the middle of the shins; what is between it and the ankles, whatever is below that is in the Fire. Allah does not look at one who drags his lower garment out of arrogance."
"2348","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Salama ibn Kuhayl informed me, from Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami, who said: My brother informed me, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-jarr, al-dubba, and al-muzaffat, and mixing unripe dates with ripe dates, meaning nabidh."
"2349","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking by inverting the waterskins. Al-Zuhri was asked: What is inverting the waterskins? He said: Drinking from their mouths."
"2350","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench, and we were distracted from prayers, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who made an iqama for each prayer. That was before there was revealed to him: {If you fear, then on foot or mounted}."
"2351","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq informed us, saying: I heard al-Agharr say: I testify concerning Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayra that they both testified concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah grants respite until two-thirds of the night have passed, then He descends and says: Is there any asker? Is there any penitent? Is there any seeker of forgiveness for a sin? A man said to him: Until dawn breaks? He said: Yes."
"2352","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, who said: I testify concerning Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayra that they both testified concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, but the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquillity descends upon them, and Allah, mighty and majestic, mentions them among those with Him."
"2353","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' and Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, from Abu Sa'id, that Ali sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gold in its dust, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it that day among four: Uyayna ibn Hisn al-Fazari, Alqama ibn Ulatha al-Kilabi, al-Aqra' ibn Habis al-Hanzali, and Zayd al-Khayl al-Ta'i, then of Banu Hazzan. Quraysh and the Ansar became angry and said: He gives the people of Najd and leaves us! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only gave them to reconcile them. Then a man stood, sunken-eyed, shaven-headed, prominent-cheeked, protruding-foreheaded, and said: Fear Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will obey Allah if I disobey Him? The people of heaven trust me and you do not trust me? Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, sought his permission to kill him, but he refused. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From the offspring of this man a people will emerge who recite the Quran without it passing their throats; they will pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the game; they will kill the people of Islam and leave the people of idols. By Allah, if I reach them I will kill them as Ad were killed."
"2354","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, who said: It was said to A'isha: Abu Sa'id says the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not travel except with a mahram relative. A'isha turned to one of those with her and said: By Allah, not all of them have a mahram."
"2355","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, who said: I heard a man of Thaqif narrating from a man of Kinana, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning this verse, {Then We caused those of Our servants whom We chose to inherit the Book}, the verse: All of them are in Paradise - or he said: All of them are of one rank. Shu'ba doubted which of the two."
"2356","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Qaraza, from Abu Sa'id, who said: I bought a ram to sacrifice, but a wolf ate its tail - or part of its tail - so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Sacrifice it."
"2357","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Qaza'a, from Abu Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Fitr and the day of Adha."
"2358","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salih, from Abu Alqama al-Hashimi, from Abu Sa'id, who said: On the day of Awtas we captured women who had husbands, and we disliked having relations with them, so we asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was revealed: {And married women except those your right hands possess}."
"2359","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrating from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Sa'd ibn Mu'adh concerning the judgment of Banu Qurayza, and he came on a donkey. When he drew near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Stand to your chief - or he said: To your best. When he came he said: Judge among them. He said: I judge among them that their fighters be killed and their offspring enslaved. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have judged with the judgment of the King."
"2360","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Muthanna and Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick and follow funerals; they remind you of the Hereafter."
"2361","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Sacrifice and the day of Fitr, and prayer after Asr and after Fajr."
"2362","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Asma ibn Ubayd, from al-Sa'ib, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These houses have dwellers, so whatever you see of them, warn it three times; whatever appears to you after that, it is a disbeliever, so kill it."
"2363","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uqba ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We were forbidden to combine raisins with dates, and unripe dates with dates, for nabidh."
"2364","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Masruq, who said: Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud was mentioned in the presence of Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he said: He is a man I will never cease to love after I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Learn the Quran from four: from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfa, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal."
"2365","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of you to me are the best of you in character. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither obscene nor deliberately obscene."
"2366","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Masruq, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Learn the Quran from four: Abd Allah, Mu'adh, Ubayy, and Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfa."
"2367","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Zur'a ibn Amr ibn Jarir, who said: We were with Abd Allah ibn Amr when two men came and said: We came to you from Marwan, and we heard him say: The first of the signs to appear is the emergence of the Dajjal. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Marwan lied; I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith I have not forgotten. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of the signs to appear is the rising of the sun from its west, or the emergence of the Beast to people in the forenoon; whichever of them comes before the other, the other follows soon after. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: And I think the first of them is the rising of the sun from its west."
"2368","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The time of Zuhr is when the sun has declined and a man's shadow is like his height, as long as Asr has not come. The time of Asr is as long as the sun has not yellowed, and the time of Maghrib is as long as the twilight has not disappeared - Shu'ba said: as long as the light of the twilight has not fallen - and the time of Isha is between you and midnight, and the time of Fajr is when dawn breaks as long as the sun has not risen. Abu Dawud said: Shu'ba sometimes raised it to the Prophet and sometimes did not raise it."
"2369","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Anbas narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us at al-Waht, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bent a finger for us and said: Kinship is a branch from the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic, joined, with an eloquent tongue speaking as it wishes; whoever joins it, Allah joins him, and whoever severs it, Allah, mighty and majestic, severs him."
"2370","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while some people were remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, and some were studying fiqh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Both gatherings are toward good; as for those who remember Allah, mighty and majestic, and ask their Lord, if He wills He gives them and if He wills He withholds from them, while these teach people and learn. I was only sent as a teacher, and this is better. So he sat with them."
"2371","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he raises his head from the last prostration then breaks his ablution, his prayer is complete."
"2372","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with silk and gold and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my community and lawful for its females."
"2373","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Abbas al-Makki - he was a poet and was not suspected concerning hadith - say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking permission for jihad, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then strive in them."
"2374","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Abbas say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have I not been told that you stand the night and fast the day? If you do that, the eye grows weary and the soul grows exhausted. One who fasts perpetually has not fasted. Fasting three days of every month is fasting the whole year. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am able. He said: Then fast the fast of Dawud, peace be upon him; he fasted a day and broke fast a day, and did not flee when he met the enemy."
"2375","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, who heard Abu al-Abbas narrating from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to recite the Quran in five days."
"2376","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a loan combined with a sale, two conditions in a sale, selling what is not with you, and profit on what you have not guaranteed."
"2377","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Khalifa al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers' blood is equal, and they are one hand against others."
"2378","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Khalifa al-Khayyat, known as Abu Hubayra, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then sees something better than it, let him do it; that is its expiation."
"2379","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Khalifa narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned his back against the Ka'ba and said: There is no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, nor after Asr until it sets."
"2380","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from a man, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat, drink, dress, and give charity, for Allah, mighty and majestic, loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant."
"2381","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhammad al-Mulayki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The fasting person has, at his breaking of fast, an answered supplication. Abd Allah ibn Amr, when he broke his fast, would call his family and children and supplicate."
"2382","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has added a prayer for you, so maintain it, and it is the Witr."
"2383","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charities of the Muslims are taken at their waters - or: at their courtyards; Abu Dawud doubted."
"2384","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership."
"2385","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: That is the lesser sodomy, meaning approaching the woman in her rear."
"2386","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, saying: Habib al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a man owns a woman, her gift is not valid except with his permission."
"2387","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of the People of the Book, Jew and Christian, is half the blood-money of the Muslim."
"2388","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the greatest sins is that a man revile his parents in Islam. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he revile his parents? He said: He exchanges insults with a man, who then reviles his father, or he reviles his mother and he reviles his mother."
"2389","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'a, from Uqba ibn Aws - Khalid thought it from Abd Allah ibn Amr - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Makkah, said: There is no god but Allah alone; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Every inherited honor claimed, and every blood and wealth, is under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the Ka'ba and the watering of pilgrims."
"2390","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Rayhan ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one possessing strength and vigor."
"2391","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra; I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrating from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor deliberate obscenity; beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever ties and they severed, commanded them to be miserly and they were miserly, commanded them to wickedness and they were wicked. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? Shu'ba said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Al-Mas'udi said: That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and hand. That man or another stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which emigration is best? He said: That you abandon what your Lord hates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Emigration is of two kinds: the emigration of the settled and the emigration of the Bedouin. As for the Bedouin, he responds when called and obeys when commanded; as for the settled, his trial is greater and his reward better. Al-Mas'udi said: And a man called to him: O Messenger of Allah, which martyrs are best? He said: That your horse be hamstrung and your blood shed."
"2392","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: In how many days do you recite the Quran? I said: In a day and two nights. He kept bargaining with me until he said: Recite it in seven."
"2393","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever claims belonging to other than his father will never smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a distance of seventy years. When Junada ibn Abi Umayya saw that - and Mu'awiya had wanted to claim him - Junada said: I am but an arrow in your quiver; shoot me where you will."
"2394","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who reads it in less than three days does not understand it, meaning the Quran."
"2395","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, saying: My maternal uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed."
"2396","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn Rafi', from Hanan ibn Kharija, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: A bold, coarse Bedouin from the highlands came and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about emigration: is it to you wherever you are, or to a known land, or to a particular people, or does it end when you die? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent, then said: Where is the asker? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Emigration is to abandon obscenities, apparent and hidden; then you are an emigrant even if you die in settled land. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the garments of the people of Paradise: are they created anew or woven? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent and some people laughed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you laugh? At an ignorant one asking a scholar?! Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is the asker? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather the fruits of Paradise split open with them - twice. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about emigration and jihad? He said: O Abd Allah, begin with yourself and campaign against it, begin with yourself and strive against it; if you are killed fleeing, Allah will raise you fleeing; if killed showing off, Allah will raise you showing off; if killed patiently seeking reward, Allah will raise you patiently seeking reward."
"2397","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two saffron-dyed garments on me and said: O Abd Allah ibn Amr, these are the garments of the disbelievers, so do not wear them."
"2398","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Ibn Uyayna narrated to us - and the hadith of Ibn Uyayna is more complete - from Amr ibn Dinar, from Suhayb, the freedman of Ibn Amir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills a sparrow without its right, Allah, mighty and majestic, will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: What is its right? He said: He slaughters it and eats it, and does not cut off its head and throw it away."
"2399","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Talha ibn Hilal - or Hilal ibn Talha - hear Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting three days of the month is fasting the whole year; whoever brings a good deed has ten like it. I said: I am able. He said: Then fast the fast of Dawud; he fasted a day and broke fast a day."
"2400","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Wahb ibn Jabir say: I witnessed Abd Allah ibn Amr in Bayt al-Maqdis when a freedman of his came to him and said: I wish to stay here this month, meaning Ramadan. Abd Allah said to him: Have you left for your family what sustains them? He said: No. He said: If not, then return and leave them what sustains them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It suffices a man as sin to neglect those he sustains."
